{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was","id":1554743,"title":"I think my issue with the Second Inquisition was...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-28T14:25:50-07:00","id":1554743,"title":"I think my issue with the Second Inquisition was...","content":"The recent thread I made on how the Second Inquisition could end had me thinking about what the intentions were for the organization versus the expectations of fans.<br /> <br /> I had a problem with THE SECOND INQUISITION book and why I realized that I'd been reading the writer's intentions all along. Basically, for a lot of fans, the Second Inquisition was this massive police state organization that would be able to track down and systematically eliminate vampires across the globe via anonymous military strikes during the day and burning the buildings down around them. It's a horrifying situation that means that vampire society has to cease to exist.<br /> <br /> It's not that.<br /> <br /> Instead, the intention seemed to be Blade-ifying the games more. Basically, heavily armed guys in a scary gas masks charging at the vampires in the middle of the night and getting into big fights where the vampires tear them apart with disciplines. They're basically a replacement for the Sabbat as disposable mooks and also primarily meant to be enemies in the video games.<br /> <br /> This is related to the Sabbat in that I believe the changes done to them aren't necessarily for the tabletop game but to establish them as disposable mooks for future video games as well as spin off properties. The SI and Sabbat existing less as characters to play and more for providing enemies in lore. It happened in Swansong as huge chunks of the game is killing SI soldiers like Selene or Bloodrayne. Now in Bloodlines 2, you get to slaughter whole swaths of Hunters and Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm right or maybe I'm wrong but the assumption is that the Hunters are there to provide the game orcs or goblins.<br /> <br /> It's not a bad thing, games need antagonists, but in the SI book you have less discussion of the politics behind the SI and more talk about light grenades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T15:02:18-07:00","id":1554744,"title":"","content":"Honestly, my first thought when I heard about the Second Inquisition was, &quot;Someone clearly wanted to make a game about military vampire hunters and has managed to backdoor that into a new edition of Vampire.&quot; But your read on them, especially the mooks-for-video-games angle, also makes sense. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T21:44:16-07:00","id":1554755,"title":"","content":"I think the two problems with this take are, first, that it assumes there <b>is</b> a clear and cohesive set of intentions behind the SI, and second that the author's intention supersedes what's actually written.<br /> <br /> This is a gameline, even the very first book was written by many hands, and with input from even more people. The intentions behind are many and sometimes messy, and they change over books.<br /> <br /> So, my take? This may be true, but first of all the idea of a harder survival-style game was definitely there in the beginning. It's overtly spelled out in the core book, that the SI makes things hard and vampires now have to be careful when using tech, or not use it at all.<br /> <br /> Did this change in other books? Yes, it did, but that's not because it wasn't the intention. It is because ideas change.<br /> <br /> More importantly, the power of the SI was actually written in the game. It's in their resources, their knowledge, their long list of successful missions, the places where they are on top. This got more complex later on, but never went away.<br /> <br /> You can downplay the SI in a chronicle. That's not by any means an issue. At any given time, at certain places, they may be little more than scary mooks to kill. But in the <i>setting</i> you can't simply say they're not dangerous without either changing the setting through new developments or retconning a lot of it. This is the setting as presented.<br /> <br /> What is the SI? It <b>is</b> a bunch of semi-competent idiots for you to kill in droves in a video game. But also, it <b>is</b> this massive police state organization that would be able to track down and systematically eliminate vampires across the globe via anonymous military strikes during the day and burning the buildings down around them. And most importantly, it is everything in between.<br /> <br /> But it's not less than this. It is a definitive change in the background danger level for vampire society however you see it, that's not going away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T01:28:23-07:00","id":1554762,"title":"","content":"<br /> I am more or less agree with you CTPhipps<br /> <br /> Personally, my main problem with the Second Inquisition is how totally unreqalistic it is even for a RPG<br /> <br /> The first Inquisition and the Burning Times that raged throughout Europe for ~200 years was a &quot;sucess&quot; becasue between the 14th century to the 16th the rule of big numbers kicked in; not all inquisitors of that time knew they were up against Vampires and other and tons of innocents burned along with &quot;monsters&quot;. It is basically accepted &quot;fact&quot; the death-toll of the Inquisition was greatly exaggerated in later periods - sure if you were alive in that time it was not the best time to live (or unlive) but it wasn't an Armageddon and the End Times either - the High Clans mostly soared thrugh it basically unmolasted with a few casualities and as always the Low Clans suffered more<br /> But you know who suffered the most?<br /> The Garou and their Kinfolk<br /> Gaia-worship was seen as heresy and witchcraft and persecuted accordingly. (and as a bonus, suddenly every &quot;wise woman&quot; became a target and the Black Furies had massive loss of kin)<br /> And to be a Verbena was mostly a death sentance - heck even a real Hunter had to keep her head low or found herself on the wrong end of the stick to burn<br /> Vampires, especially the Cappadocian, Salubri and Lasombra had a very Strong influence in the Church (both Cappadocius and the Capuchin had and still have acces to the Vatican' Secret Archives for example)<br /> Sury it was a tragedy, the Vampires self-image was shook and many died but it wasn't &quot;that bad&quot; the most of the Elders paint it to be and sure it was partially responsible for the formation of the Camarilla but the sect's birth was more of the result of the Anarch Revolt that threatened the Cainite domains throughout Europe than the threat of the Inquisition - but of course it was responsible too, but it was more of an added excuse in my humble oppinion to tighten that leash the Princes and Elders already had<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition?<br /> <br /> What was the premise?<br /> The intelligence agencies of the United States managed to gain access to SchreckNet &quot;somehow&quot; and gained firsthand knowledge of the existence of Vampires and they shared their knowledge with other intelligence agencies then contacted the Vatican, whom they knew to have experience fighting the undead.<br /> Wait for a second\u2026 the KNEW the Vatican had experience fighting the undead\u2026 so\u2026 by extention the existance of undead too?<br /> Okay, move on<br /> After years - YEARS - of careful research, the Coalition had targeted Vienna as the &quot;capital of vampires&quot; and prepared a strike against their headquarters and in 2008 stormed the Vienna Chantry and destroyed the foudnation of Clan Tremere - with presumably the destruction of the Inner Council of Seven, Blood Bonds were shattered. Tremere fell from gray eminences to personae non gratae in many regions.<br /> And io and behold... the Salubri resurfaced<br /> Now tell me it wasn't Saulot's/Salubri plot.. or a conspiracy to get rid of the Tremere<br /> But okay, lets assume it was all by the Humans without any outside influence and they got lucky<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition is kind of a joke if you think about it, as CTPhipps said with tons of problems<br /> <br /> They built their whole operations on the information they gathere from the SchreckNet and/then from electronic devices like phones mails ,etc<br /> While knowing from the said informations - especially from the SchreckNet - both SchreckNet 1.0 and SchreckNet 2.0 (and other Nosferatu information networks (such as Trajan's Net) are maintained by Vampires - even if they don't know the Nosferatu, you have to be a special kind of idiot to not realize, the undead community built a Network... they are kind of experts<br /> And you want to use that\u2026 and other networks<br /> <br /> See the problem?<br /> <br /> They are ripe to be fooled and aimed at the right directions (and to be fair in London? Exactly that happened) to be used as tools\u2026<br /> <br /> And even V5 admitted, the Camarilla run counter-intelligence in Washington and Brussels and they just returned to the &quot;old school&quot; spycraft, skills vampires mastered way before the time the Borgias conspired against cardinals and kings\u2026 with a healthy Animalism usage (so basically the Nosferatu are back in their old busienss and curriers)<br /> <br /> And the Anarchs? Many just ended up as SI consultants\u2026<br /> Not that great, but ultimatelly play to the Camarilla's hand to justify they are traitors of their kind<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know what was the intention, but if you think about it, and in my oppinion the Second Inqusition nothing more than an uncomfortable excuse and not even that usefull tool in the arsenal of Vampires<br /> <br /> But a real threat that you really have to take seriously?<br /> <br /> No, not really","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-29-2025, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T19:41:56-07:00","id":1554809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554762#post1554762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, my main problem with the Second Inquisition is how totally unreqalistic it is even for a RPG</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. But that's not the point.<br /> <br /> They're written as a global threat, they affect the setting as a global threat.<br /> <br /> Being badly written, unrealistic or hard to take seriously doesn't change what the official books say they do.<br /> <br /> In the context of the previous thread mentioned, what the designers did to the setting was to establish this super-threat, regardless if it is convincing or not.<br /> <br /> And in the context of the OP... as non-serious and incompetent as you can picture them, this is definitely not the design intention behind them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T20:02:01-07:00","id":1554813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554809#post1554809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And in the context of the OP... as non-serious and incompetent as you can picture them, this is definitely not the design intention behind them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see them as non-serious or non-competent but I see them as goons. Goons who will attack the PCs at night in tactical armor and get into huge John Wick action scenes with them. Because the goal is to create a more action-heavy game that the new rules will have extremely quick combat with and the PCs having decided advantages.<br /> <br /> And my evidence to this is the massive focus on stats, equipment, and battle scenes in the sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> I could well be seeing them wrong but I don't think I am.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T21:16:08-07:00","id":1554822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554813#post1554813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see them as non-serious or non-competent but I see them as goons. Goons who will attack the PCs at night in tactical armor and get into huge John Wick action scenes with them. Because the goal is to create a more action-heavy game that the new rules will have extremely quick combat with and the PCs having decided advantages.<br /> <br /> And my evidence to this is the massive focus on stats, equipment, and battle scenes in the sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> I could well be seeing them wrong but I don't think I am.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was addressing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> still, he said it, not you.<br /> <br /> And I don't think you're wrong, actually you're probably right, I think you're incomplete.<br /> <br /> They're not <i>either</i> a massive threat or a mass of goons, they're <i><b>both</b></i> a massive threat and a mass of goons. And a few other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T11:59:45-07:00","id":1554859,"title":"","content":"In fact the Second Inquisition is no more and no less than what your table needs them to be - like any other element of a tabletop game setting.<br /> <br /> For the record, I think that depicting the Second Inquisition as an order of magnitude more successful and effective than the original makes perfect sense - it\u2019s a way to emphasise that rational secularism and centuries of technological progress make Humanity far more dangerous than they were back in the \u2018Dark Ages\u2019 in a way that VAMPIRE sourcebooks had been noting for some while but never previously demonstrated.<br /> <br /> (It also seems fair to point out that while the Licks who put Shreck,bet together are experts, their field of expertise is sufficiently young that rival human experts are still operating on a level playing field - especially since the \u2018Mere Mortals\u2019 don\u2019t have to worry so much about an especially cranky Elder deciding to play State Security).<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I can\u2019t lie, seeing Humanity light up the Kindred for once is something my Van Helsing-loving heart delights in: the Second Inquisition is a valuable reminder that vampires are no more the Lords of the Night than a black panther (In that they\u2019re dangerous and predatory creatures, but far from invincible).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T13:13:54-07:00","id":1554867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554859#post1554859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact the Second Inquisition is no more and no less than what your table needs them to be - like any other element of a tabletop game setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that's a discussion-killing argument.<br /> <br /> We all know we can ignore the books and do whatever. Many of us have plenty of experience doing so.<br /> <br /> But discussing the setting means discussing what's officially in the books, because that's the common ground we have. Otherwise it's completely pointless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, I think that depicting the Second Inquisition as an order of magnitude more successful and effective than the original makes perfect sense - it\u2019s a way to emphasise that rational secularism and centuries of technological progress make Humanity far more dangerous than they were back in the \u2018Dark Ages\u2019 in a way that VAMPIRE sourcebooks had been noting for some while but never previously demonstrated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally think the books did showed this previously.<br /> <br /> Since 1st edition, all a mortal needs to be a big, real problem is to know enough about you and be about during the day. A mortal can literally bulldoze your Haven. Bring a flamethrower to a fight. Use assault rifles and hand grenades.<br /> <br /> Technology is more powerful than Disciplines, hands down. In the Middle Ages you could have a stone castle and be pretty safe against mortals even if they knew about you, nowadays that's far from enough.<br /> <br /> Classic VtM is about vampires living as the secret masters of the world, that ultimately must remain secret because collective Humanity is just too dangerous. By the way, the Technocracy does not have nearly enough nukes to eliminate every Ante, <u><b>but Russia and the US have</b></u>. Direct domination simply isn't an option. And hunters have always existed, plenty of them, all with the resources to make things hard for vampire even if they can't hope to survive a direct confrontation with an Elder.<br /> <br /> What the SI does is to increase the background danger to a degree where vampires aren't even in control anymore, as the SI is the one in control of military assets around the world.<br /> <br /> You can add nuance to this? Surely. Is it simple and homogeneous? Definitely not. But it is a fundamentally distinct premise for the game, even if they're now mostly ignoring it because they want to pretend this is Classic VtM.<br /> <br /> And I personally find that the biggest problem with the SI (and with most setting changes from the beginning of V5) isn't that it exists, but that Paradox wanted to make big moves, but not commit to them.<br /> <br /> V5 shouldn't try to be Masquerade as usual, it should thoroughly embrace its own identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T14:24:05-07:00","id":1554873,"title":"","content":"IMO part of the problem is that the second inquistion is treated as a plot device for railroading rather than a functional faction<br /> <br /> -They wanted the Tremere to be more diverse so they nuked Vienna<br /> <br /> -They don't like you using tech so they had the Cam do a tech ban in response (which would actually make the situation worse)<br /> <br /> But for some reason the game still more of less looks like a mid 90's vtm game<br /> <br /> They really do feel like a wasted opportunity and it doesn't help that theirs like 2 additional world changing events going on at the same time.<br /> <br /> Thinking on it the 2nd inq should probably be winding down now since either most kindred would be dead or the Tower would have 'won'.<br /> <br /> -","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T14:29:43-07:00","id":1554874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554873#post1554873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO part of the problem is that the second inquistion is treated as a plot device for railroading rather than a functional faction</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that they also cleansed Mexico City and Montreal because they wanted to do Camarilla games there.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I give them a pass on this because if you have Mexico City and Montreal fan clubs there then you should go with the fandom.<br /> <br /> <b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -They don't like you using tech so they had the Cam do a tech ban in response (which would actually make the situation worse) </div> </div> </div></b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - </div> </div> </div>I am so cynical I truly believe this is so they can have the pneumatic tube system of John Wick and other stuff from that movie to make the Camarilla look more analog/Dieselpunk. You know, switchboards and shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T15:30:08-07:00","id":1554879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554874#post1554874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget that they also cleansed Mexico City and Montreal because they wanted to do Camarilla games there.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I give them a pass on this because if you have Mexico City and Montreal fan clubs there then you should go with the fandom.<br /> <br /> [B]<br /> <br /> I am so cynical I truly believe this is so they can have the pneumatic tube system of John Wick and other stuff from that movie to make the Camarilla look more analog/Dieselpunk. You know, switchboards and shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like the last thing that the directives behind V5 would have promoted was the tone and themes of John Wick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T15:42:45-07:00","id":1554880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554879#post1554879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like the last thing that the directives behind V5 would have promoted was the tone and themes of John Wick.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think?<br /> <br /> I think it was a good reference for modern WOD. I remember when we had those recommendations in the backs of the books. I miss em.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T16:12:52-07:00","id":1554881,"title":"","content":"Whatever the intent behind the SI is doesn't really matter in the face of the in book actual execution of the SI, where over and over the material gives them capabilities and achievements that make &quot;how are there any vampires anymore&quot; unavoidable and the idea that anyone could get away with being a vampire rock star anymore (the whole ass premise of an upcoming book) hysterical.<br /> <br /> And &quot;well there are vampires secretly helping them along!&quot; excuses nothing when the books themselves repeatedly near verbatim state that the SI are an ultimately inescapable force that can kill all vampires. The SI book itself has a specific section noting that, for all that other sections don't<br /> <br /> The problem now is they're basically incoherent, because the line itself is at this point basically incoherent. The SI need to be a terrifying multiple city ending, Vienna bombing force whose only reason for not having tracked your pc down is they haven't gotten around to you yet. But you also need to be able to somehow play your vampire rockstar pc because oops Interview with the Vampire is popular again and also the extremely narrow focus of V5 ran out of ideas after five or so years, as evidenced by how much they have been doing things they swore they never would and mocked the idea of from the outset (playing older vampires, having an entire book on love and fucking, having something that almost feels like a metaplot book, etc. etc. etc.)<br /> <br /> edit: Yes, I've certainly griped in bunches about how narrow V5 is, and even punitive to straying outside its focus, both in mechanics and setting, but you can't spend years reinforcing being that narrow, having some of your onetime devs say how great it is to be that narrow, and then just act like no, you can totally do all this other stuff without even acknowledging the issue, either in system or setting, without making things into a big ol mess. The SI and all their problems is emblematic of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 10-30-2025, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T17:23:35-07:00","id":1554882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554874#post1554874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget that they also cleansed Mexico City and Montreal because they wanted to do Camarilla games there.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I give them a pass on this because if you have Mexico City and Montreal fan clubs there then you should go with the fandom.<br /> <br /> [B]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An odd mindset on a number of levels. Im not ever clear on the internal logic here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T17:34:26-07:00","id":1554883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554882#post1554882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> An odd mindset on a number of levels. Im not ever clear on the internal logic here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Montreal Game Studio wants to make CHAPTERS.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, can we set it in Montreal?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We need to make it a Camarilla city.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T18:11:08-07:00","id":1554884,"title":"","content":"Yes, both in Montreal and in Mexico City the local fandom (at least the most outspoken members) makes them Cam cities. I agree that following their lead is a nice thing to do.<br /> <br /> But there's no reason for this to be done with the SI cleansing the cities.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite, the idea that they cleansed so thoroughly and then just left completely is hard to swallow. The most obvious thing would be that once free of local vampires they would attract newcomers. Both the SI would keep heavy vigilance and the Cam would expect so.<br /> <br /> Add the whole problem of vampires traveling in the first place, and droves of newcomers simply coming and building their society no prob is quite contrived. Not impossible, but stretching it a lot.<br /> <br /> Hadn't the Sabbat left for the Middle East anyways? Couldn't the Cam just take the cities from their leftovers as usual? Wouldn't it make a lot more sense to have a local Cam community that was preparing in hiding and then overtook the city instead of everyone coming from the outside to occupy a place that just got vamp-nuked by militaristic murder-hobos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T01:56:10-07:00","id":1554889,"title":"","content":"Odd considering their deliberate antipathy for large numbers of players (Sabbat players for example) in general that they'd specifically alter setting details to humor sections of the community. Although the Montreal rationalisation makes sense as brand expansion is a higher priority than setting concerns.<br /> <br /> As a side between the Sabbat exodus, the 2nd inquistion and the beckoning, depopulation should be on a scale were the settings closer to the long night than anything. Realistically their should'nt even be an Anarch revolt because resource competition just divebombed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-31-2025, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T14:07:53-07:00","id":1554898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554889#post1554889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd considering their deliberate antipathy for large numbers of players (Sabbat players for example) in general that they'd specifically alter setting details to humor sections of the community. Although the Montreal rationalisation makes sense as brand expansion is a higher priority than setting concerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not 100% devoted to my theory that the &quot;action-ification&quot; of White Wolf was a specific goal for 5th edition but I think that the Sabbat's changes were designed around the probability of making them antagonists for future games that didn't really require much thinking about killing. The Sabbat in the Modern Day have been distilled down to their most basic faceless horde. This isn't 100% bad storytelling as the Sabbat degenerating in their humanity and becoming shadows of their former selves is actually something that fits the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> But I suspect there's another possible angle for the reason the Sabbat were moved from PC to NPC status, it's possible they also intended to try to avoid some controversy. The Sabbat are diabolical religious terrorists who engage in all manner of nastiness. It could be that Paradox just wanted to avoid the kind of controversies that had accompanied the Ventrue who fed on children and other early issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a side between the Sabbat exodus, the 2nd inquistion and the beckoning, depopulation should be on a scale were the settings closer to the long night than anything. Realistically their should'nt even be an Anarch revolt because resource competition just divebombed. </div> </div> </div>I think the implications have been in-universe that there was a &quot;Baby Boom&quot; in the 2000s and that the number of Embracees in the present far outstrip the previous numbers before, partially because of Anarchs and partially because Thin Bloods breed like rabbits. Which is why suddenly we have so many Princes like Hazel Iverson, Kevin Jackson, and even Prince Campbell who are barely Ancilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T14:28:24-07:00","id":1554899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554884#post1554884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, both in Montreal and in Mexico City the local fandom (at least the most outspoken members) makes them Cam cities. I agree that following their lead is a nice thing to do.<br /> <br /> But there's no reason for this to be done with the SI cleansing the cities.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite, the idea that they cleansed so thoroughly and then just left completely is hard to swallow. The most obvious thing would be that once free of local vampires they would attract newcomers. Both the SI would keep heavy vigilance and the Cam would expect so.<br /> <br /> Add the whole problem of vampires traveling in the first place, and droves of newcomers simply coming and building their society no prob is quite contrived. Not impossible, but stretching it a lot.<br /> <br /> Hadn't the Sabbat left for the Middle East anyways? Couldn't the Cam just take the cities from their leftovers as usual? Wouldn't it make a lot more sense to have a local Cam community that was preparing in hiding and then overtook the city instead of everyone coming from the outside to occupy a place that just got vamp-nuked by militaristic murder-hobos?</div> </div> </div> </div>This comes to the issue I had over in the &quot;How the Second Inquisition Will End&quot; and the question of logistics for the organization. Basically, a lot of organizations in video games or movies have the Tv tropes &quot;Offscreen Dark Matter&quot; where they seemingly have unlimited resources to have things like Blofeld's Volcano Lair or whatever.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition being an actually secret organization in the United States and other places means that they will have at least some form of accountability, if for no reason that they're maintaining their own form of the Masquerade. People will notice if too many members start dying, billions get wasted, and large amounts of information are being assembled for no reason (that part they can outsource to private companies)<br /> <br /> So the SI can't possibly be the kind of global all powerful organization it is sometimes depicted as being and its numbers should be far smaller than the game sometimes acts like they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T16:17:24-07:00","id":1554900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554898#post1554898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not 100% devoted to my theory that the &quot;action-ification&quot; of White Wolf was a specific goal for 5th edition but I think that the Sabbat's changes were designed around the probability of making them antagonists for future games that didn't really require much thinking about killing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite possible.<br /> <br /> But for the matter at hand, their cities, what's important is that they left them <i>en masse</i>, regardless of why the authors did this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554898#post1554898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't 100% bad storytelling as the Sabbat degenerating in their humanity and becoming shadows of their former selves is actually something that fits the themes of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat is already a shadow of its former Anarch Revolt self, the Paths in particular are shadows of the old Roads.<br /> <br /> And in the context of an RPG game their oversimplification only removes options, it doesn't really play out that well as a degeneration trope. There were many better ways of working this idea out without doing what they did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554898#post1554898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I suspect there's another possible angle for the reason the Sabbat were moved from PC to NPC status, it's possible they also intended to try to avoid some controversy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dumb, but also probable.<br /> <br /> Especially because I think they're trying to not alienate far-right players, and those would hate the fact that the big villains are a well-thought, complex and nuanced sect of extremist Christians.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554898#post1554898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the implications have been in-universe that there was a &quot;Baby Boom&quot; in the 2000s and that the number of Embracees in the present far outstrip the previous numbers before, partially because of Anarchs and partially because Thin Bloods breed like rabbits. Which is why suddenly we have so many Princes like Hazel Iverson, Kevin Jackson, and even Prince Campbell who are barely Ancilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fair assumptions, but then again we have the problem of Paradox wanting big changes without committing to them.<br /> <br /> We have nothing in the books stating that vampire demography significantly changed recently, or that most of them are new. And 2000 to now is quite young for a vampire, much less for most of a city's vampire population, imagine when V5 was released.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day they made a context that heavily implies that demography, but never used it for real in writing. And it isn't a small thing, that changes a lot of how the game plays out.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the SI can't possibly be the kind of global all powerful organization it is sometimes depicted as being and its numbers should be far smaller than the game sometimes acts like they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less, but I mostly agree. My point in that thread is more that the authors wrote then like that than it necessarily making a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> But for what matters here, keeping vigilance on those cities isn't hard. As a conspiracy within governments the SI can access a lot of institutional resources without the need to own them.<br /> <br /> So leaving behind people in positions to inform strange occurrences isn't hard (they don't need to know what they're looking for, or for whom really it is), and they don't need to put cameras all over the place themselves, just at key points, and otherwise be informed if other cameras get something.<br /> <br /> You can make something as simple as leaving a local government department with instructions to gather reports on camera malfunctions, specifically citing thermal cameras that aren't getting the heat of some people. Paint it as merely quality control for industry standards, and now virtually every thermal camera in the city is working for you, even if it takes some time for the reports to come.<br /> <br /> The problem with this kind of situation is that the SI has the simple advantage that they only have to get you once, while you have to live in hiding all the time, &quot;forever&quot;.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T21:02:53-07:00","id":1554908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554900#post1554900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite possible. But for the matter at hand, their cities, what's important is that they left them <i>en masse</i>, regardless of why the authors did this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Sabbat losing their cities is just so everything can be Camarilla-ized or Anarch-ized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat is already a shadow of its former Anarch Revolt self, the Paths in particular are shadows of the old Roads. </div> </div> </div>I actually thought this was the endpoint of where they were already headed as of Revised.<br /> <br /> FYI - I recommend THE SABBAT book on the Storyteller's Vault as I got a review copy and it's basically 700 pages of adapting not only the Sabbat but the Black Hand, True Black Hand, and a bunch of other occult groups to the modern day. They basically act like the Sabbat of 5th Edition is a breakaway sect of murderous lunatics while Lucita is the regent of the &quot;normal&quot; Sabbat that is heavily involved in Gehenna occultism and lore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially because I think they're trying to not alienate far-right players, and those would hate the fact that the big villains are a well-thought, complex and nuanced sect of extremist Christians. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's the case since Jason Carl's famous, &quot;Nazi Players fuck off&quot; article. The Sabbat are also Satanic in their handling of their religion and are only similar if you don't see opposites of the same religion as that different (&quot;Jedi and Sith are the same.&quot;). I think that it's more meant to try to avoid the general controversy that dogged a lot of reboots but is probably actually unavoidable. I could be completely off base, though. The funny thing about V:TM is it avoided a bunch of the Satanic panic because it was so much more niche than D&amp;D and the majority of people panicking about D&amp;D never understood what it was that well to begin with let alone knowing V:TM was much darker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a fair assumptions, but then again we have the problem of Paradox wanting big changes without committing to them. </div> </div> </div>Point taken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We have nothing in the books stating that vampire demography significantly changed recently, or that most of them are new. And 2000 to now is quite young for a vampire, much less for most of a city's vampire population, imagine when V5 was released. </div> </div> </div>We do have the Beckoning significantly changing the demographics. I think Paradox was actually somewhat annoyed with how many Elders were in books like FALL OF LONDON and CHICAGO BY NIGHT. Mind you, they were the ones who left Tegyrius and Victoria Ash as Unbeckoned with no reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More or less, but I mostly agree. My point in that thread is more that the authors wrote then like that than it necessarily making a lot of sense. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But for what matters here, keeping vigilance on those cities isn't hard. As a conspiracy within governments the SI can access a lot of institutional resources without the need to own them.<br /> <br /> So leaving behind people in positions to inform strange occurrences isn't hard (they don't need to know what they're looking for, or for whom really it is), and they don't need to put cameras all over the place themselves, just at key points, and otherwise be informed if other cameras get something.<br /> <br /> You can make something as simple as leaving a local government department with instructions to gather reports on camera malfunctions, specifically citing thermal cameras that aren't getting the heat of some people. Paint it as merely quality control for industry standards, and now virtually every thermal camera in the city is working for you, even if it takes some time for the reports to come.<br /> <br /> The problem with this kind of situation is that the SI has the simple advantage that they only have to get you once, while you have to live in hiding all the time, &quot;forever&quot;.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Possibly but I'm not so sure. It really depends on how many people we think are actually in the Second Inquisition and it's various organizations. FIRSTLIGHT, The Entity, Special Affairs Division, the Inquisition, the Arcanum, and so on are all cooperating for the first time but they're still all technically separate. They also have a bunch of hunter orgs that are being loosely used by them as canon fodder if WINTER'S TEETH (The Mortician's Army) and the local hunters in Chicago were. Basically, without suggesting they're a bunch of disunited groups with common cause *cough* Vigils *cough*, they may well be a lot less structures than they seem.<br /> <br /> Mind you, when I ran the Technocracy, I had an agent explain that the Technocracy wasn't NEARLY as large as it appeared but was operating a Pyramid Scheme. They didn't assemble the master databases on Tradition mages that made them seem omniscient. They just had access to social security numbers, police records, the NSA, and so on that they used to profile people. It's very easy to say X character is a terrorist and get local cooperation versus doing the legwork yourself. The cops who are shooting at you don't know you're a mage.<br /> <br /> I think I got that from The Matrix but it's an easy idea to have.<br /> <br /> &quot;No, your men are already dead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T08:17:07-07:00","id":1554914,"title":"","content":"It might be too topical today but well before the present, I'd also been thinking about the Second Inquisition and private funding.<br /> <br /> In the fantastic video game, ALPHA PROTOCOL, one of the interesting things was all the Tom Clancy craziness had to be justified. The game made a point that the various super secret spy agencies had to find alternate revenue streams and had the nickname, &quot;Yellow Brick Roading.&quot; Them being criminal spy agencies, they mostly did this via insider trading and setting up proxy companies that they leeched off of. The main plot of the game was doing a bunch of criminal enterprises for a big Haliburton-esque military contractor that was going to cause WW3 due to flawed predictions.<br /> <br /> While they seemed silly to me twenty years ago, I think Pentex would be more interesting to play a bigger role in the World of Darkness and integrated across the board. They would also make a good patron for the Second Inquisition despite (and because of) their vampire ties. Groups like Endron and Magadon Drugs writing big checks to the SI to help make their enemies sweat and provide them with people (Blood Dolls to ghouls to Thin Bloods) to experiment on for example. Maybe the wars would also disrupt the control of the Camarilla and other groups to increase their own power.<br /> <br /> Would they eventually turn the SI against werewolves? Well, that's a big grenade to throw in the middle of the woods but we know the SI already knows werewolves exist from Swansong. Maybe that would be part of their larger plan. <br /> <br /> Perhaps this corruption of the SI's purpose might alert the Society of Leopold and Arcanum something is seriously wrong with their government allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T10:51:32-07:00","id":1554917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554914#post1554914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While they seemed silly to me twenty years ago, I think Pentex would be more interesting to play a bigger role in the World of Darkness and integrated across the board. They would also make a good patron for the Second Inquisition despite (and because of) their vampire ties. Groups like Endron and Magadon Drugs writing big checks to the SI to help make their enemies sweat and provide them with people (Blood Dolls to ghouls to Thin Bloods) to experiment on for example. Maybe the wars would also disrupt the control of the Camarilla and other groups to increase their own power.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would make sense actually<br /> Harold Zettler, a 5th generation Malkavian antitribu was placed on the Pentex Board of Directors in a partnership between Pentex Incorporated and the Sabbat that formed in 1945<br /> And since then Zettler was pretty active<br /> Even if the Beconing/Gehenna War made him left , his Child, Persephone Tar-Anis, who was/is Pentex's North American Security chief could still play a large part<br /> It would fit, Persephone was fascinated with computers and has access to the Digital Web via a telepathic link to her sire... would explain why and how the intelligence agencies of the United States managed to gain access to SchreckNet<br /> And the Second Inquistion cleared out those who bothered the the Sabbat the most, Camarilla vampires, the infernal nest of Montreal, the clusterfuck that Mexico become (tho' I think in a setting where the Baali are a thing, Nergal/ Huitzilopochtli would have stirred from that move...)<br /> Financial backing, weapons, experimental drugs, a few fomori here and there, the Second Inquisiton teams are ideal target for the Pentex to use them<br /> Bonus points for another member of Pentex Board of Directors, Enzo Giovanni, who disappeared... but a figure calling itself Enzo Giovanni has made its appearance, but it bears no resemblance to the former large-framed vampire with the jovial bearing. Instead, it is a shriveled corpse-like husk wearing a too-large suit, but with his knowledge<br /> A Harbringer/Hecata influence would be interesting on the Second Inquisiton, keeping in mind the Capuchin had/have extraordinary connections within the Catholic Church including but not limited to access to the Vatican's library of hidden books...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554914#post1554914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would they eventually turn the SI against werewolves? Well, that's a big grenade to throw in the middle of the woods but we know the SI already knows werewolves exist from Swansong. Maybe that would be part of their larger plan.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this corruption of the SI's purpose might alert the Society of Leopold and Arcanum something is seriously wrong with their government allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vampires could be a test run or more like molding the Second Inquistion something usefull against the werewolves<br /> Weapons, combat stims, slow corruption... dangerous missions.... a testing ground for future First Team members\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T22:41:32-08:00","id":1554999,"title":"","content":"I wrote a lot, even more than my normal, then lost everything. Hence giving it two days to cool off and try again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554908#post1554908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually thought this was the endpoint of where they were already headed as of Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> In <i>Revised</i> they're spiritually and philosophically a far cry from their origins, but in the height of their <u>power</u>, <i><b>and that's the point</b></i>.<br /> <br /> At this point they're an allegory for a Christian <i>cult</i> (although not perfect), the war on the Ancients is mere propaganda. The Paths, their institutions, their ritae, everything evolved into a form that serves the purposes of their leadership (Elders, by the way), fomenting loyalty and keeping them working.<br /> <br /> This corruption of their original state is their degeneration, and the endpoint is power and wealth for their Elders. They still have a lot of what made them the Sabbat in the first place, so they still have a lot to lose, and if they stay in course they'll become just a new flavor of Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Giving up their extensive secular power and wealth to become a wandering army goes against this to become a straw-man of themselves, above all it misses the point of their allegory and their evolution. It takes the propaganda at face value to become something that isn't either point of the spectrum, but a hollow mockery of itself.<br /> <br /> One thing must be clear: the Sabbat is not an allegory on terrorism. Vampire is from 1991, cults were a far more pressing matter than terrorism. And, in fact, they still are, although this is only being noticed by people again very recently. They're not <i>Al-Qaeda</i>, they're <i>QAnon</i>. And even for a terrorism group they missed a lot of how terrorists actually work, to make what <i>politicians say</i> terrorist groups are like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">FYI - I recommend THE SABBAT book on the Storyteller's Vault</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I actually have a very distinct version of the setting for the current times in my games, so I'm mostly served with making my own stuff.<br /> <br /> Yet I plan on eventually getting it, I just have too many other things first in the backlog for now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's the case since Jason Carl's famous, &quot;Nazi Players fuck off&quot; article.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, this is just PR. Even Nazis do that nowadays when they're not being openly Nazis, and I don't mean just fascists or right-wing, I mean Nazis.<br /> <br /> Corporate talk isn't ideological, because corporations don't do ideology with their public stances, they do with their actions and their money.<br /> <br /> In their case, it's more about giving those players what they want out of the game, or not making the game offensive to them. And they don't care about what you overtly do to declared Nazis, they know it can't be helped.<br /> <br /> Now, I may be wrong. But their PR declarations mean nothing in this regard.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat are also Satanic in their handling of their religion</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, not so simple.<br /> <br /> First it's not about how they read scripture, but their attitude about it in the first place. They are Christians, they defend Christianity, they fight what they perceive as enemies of the faith when it comes to it. The worse thing for the Sabbat isn't the Ancients or the Camarilla, it's actually Infernalism, and while there are a number of Infernalists within their ranks they live in secret and fear, because the party line is no mercy, no compromise, no tolerance in any way, shape or form.<br /> <br /> Second, what you call &quot;Satanic&quot;? In the Hebrew bible &quot;\u015b\u0101\u1e6d\u0101n&quot; is actually a title for a role of &quot;prosecutor, opposer&quot;, an entity that either tests or the faithful or argues against them, with Ha-Satan being a title for the angel that mainly holds this role. This is literally what the Sabbat do and do in direct service to YHWH. Actual enemies of YHWH are their enemies too.<br /> <br /> Whatever you think of their religion and their theology, the point is that they believe in the Christian faith and follow it as they understand it. This is being Christian.<br /> <br /> Actual &quot;Satanic&quot; religions don't do that. Instead they defend some version of &quot;Satan was vilified by Christians&quot; and worship this figure instead of YHWH.<br /> <br /> I'm not arguing theology and their role within their beliefs, I'm arguing religious identity. They identify as Christians, interpret Christian scripture and dialogue with other Christian groups. This is what being Christian means from a sociological/thematic standpoint.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The funny thing about V:TM is it avoided a bunch of the Satanic panic because it was so much more niche than D&amp;D and the majority of people panicking about D&amp;D never understood what it was that well to begin with let alone knowing V:TM was much darker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe where you live, definitely not everywhere.<br /> <br /> Vampire was not that niche. During its heyday it was very famous, if only as the strange game of those goth kids. What made it miss the worse of the Satanic Panic in part of the US is that the Satanic Panic was in the 80s, by the 90s it was starting to cool down, so when Vampire became widely known it was getting the milder version of it.<br /> <br /> Also it helped that Vampire didn't had demons, not overtly. The Baali would only be mentioned in 1992 in the <i>Storyteller Handbook</i>, but worked for real only starting in 1996 with DA. Demons had far more sway with the Panic than pop-culture legends, even if they were monsters.<br /> <br /> In Brazil the Satanic Panic arrived a little later, and Vampire ended up being its main target, and I hear it happened like that in some other countries, including in the rich parts of Europe. For many reasons, around here it ended up being far more linked to Vampire than to D&amp;D, but on the other hand the problem with D&amp;D persisted. A lot of Churches still make a point of bashing any game that has demons, and D&amp;D describe them a lot, while Vampire still don't do much with them (only, if that, with infernalists).<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We do have the Beckoning significantly changing the demographics</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but then we get to their &quot;changing, but not committing to it&quot;.<br /> <br /> First they didn't change it to the point of most vampires being recent Embraces, they run a version where a lot of vampires in a city are still Ancillae, or otherwise older than 2000, as by the start of V5 you can still have Neonates from as early as the 60s.<br /> <br /> Second, they re-add Elders almost immediately, because they don't want to really make the setting work differently from what it would otherwise, and that's my problem. For all intents and purposes the demographics changed, but it's never really described as such and it has none of the impact it should have on vampire society, only the vague idea of a power vacuum that isn't ever really that important when it's even real.<br /> <br /> They basically change the setting far less than <i>Revised</i> changed Mage with a very similar plot point.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly but I'm not so sure. It really depends on how many people we think are actually in the Second Inquisition and it's various organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you actually understood my example.<br /> <br /> Keeping an eye in a city they <i>already completely wiped out of vampires</i> is easy precisely because it doesn't require a lot of resources or manpower. It's exactly what you just described of the Technocracy, you only have to use the systems a city already have in place and a little push here and there. You only need a small watch post with one or two contacts (not even actual hunters) and an excuse for them to be there.<br /> <br /> And mind you, we start this under the assumption that this organization, no matter how fractured or whatever, just wiped out all vampires of a major city under their command. This is huge, so the idea that this organization can't keep even <i>minimal</i> scrutiny afterwards is hard to believe. And as important as this, the idea that the Camarilla set up shop almost immediately after without any regard for this risk, when this number of vampires coming from the outside at once is already a hard thing to happen.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of things besides the lack of vigilance by the SI that must happen in a very specific and unlikely way to justify the Cam societies that formed in those two cities. And while none of them is strictly impossible, it's just A LOT of unlikely events in succession, making it quite contrived with no further explanation. And it happened twice.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I got that from The Matrix but it's an easy idea to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but it could very well have been from the books, because that's mostly how the Technocracy works in any book that actually describes it.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While they seemed silly to me twenty years ago, I think Pentex</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex was silly. It was silly by design, always have been.<br /> <br /> Their main narrative role is to play on office-comedy. It's not the <i><b>only</b></i> thing they do, but it's their main shtick.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pentex would be more interesting to play a bigger role in the World of Darkness and integrated across the board.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were doing that. The whole SPD debacle in the Syndicate was about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would also make a good patron for the Second Inquisition</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad idea, although not necessarily only them.<br /> <br /> A lot of people in-the-know about vampires and with stakes on their assets could be financing the SI.<br /> <br /> I'd back down from making this an official thing just because this brings potential changes to the game that won't be for every game. This kind of relationship changes a lot on how the game runs and the themes it brings once this layer of the conspiracy starts to be peeled. A broader and more generic set of bakers may give it the Financial Conspiracy twist without changing that much on the basic assumptions of a regular game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps this corruption of the SI's purpose might alert the Society of Leopold and Arcanum something is seriously wrong with their government allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't count on that. This ignores a lot about what those groups represent.<br /> <br /> Neither the Society of Leopold nor the Arcanum are truly &quot;moral&quot; as we would understand it in the setting.<br /> <br /> The Society of Leopold is a group of religious zealots. Their worldview is hyper-focused on the idea of ridding the world of the servants of the Devil as they understand it. They have no interest in understanding broader or more complex social matters, only the interests of the Church as <u>they</u> understand them. Having rich benefactors is par of the course for such groups, and fighting pagans and heretics is well within their purview. They are, by design, ultimately incapable of discerning their real enemies.<br /> <br /> And the Arcanum ultimately isn't neither invested in a particular stance nor privy to every supernatural secret in the world. They don't know about Pentex, and are unlikely to care beyond curiosity about their supernatural ties if they find out. They don't really know enough to recognize the Wyrm or its tools, this is not their thing. And things get worse with a version of the Arcane that's in the SI, which goes against the organization as previously thought. This Arcane is even less likley to know anything about spiritual corruption of any kind.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T00:39:32-08:00","id":1555008,"title":"","content":"The default vampire hunter organization being 'the feds' instead of 'the catholic church' probably makes more sense 2025 than 1900 during the Bram Stokers Dracula days. Oppressive bureaucracy probably feels closer to home than supernatural damnation.<br /> <br /> I look at the S.I, I ignore most of what the book says about them, and then I feel like I have interesting options to riff on. Like Leopold I wouldn't use them for most games though.<br /> <br /> How many of you run S.I, or Leopold? How often?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T01:22:21-08:00","id":1555012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555008#post1555008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many of you run S.I, or Leopold? How often?</div> </div> </div> </div>SI is not the feds. It is a coalition. St Leopold is a part of this coalition, if you use them, you're using the SI.<br /> <br /> If you're running those organizations as completely independent and unrelated, not sharing resources or info at any relevant level, then you're not using the SI, even if you're using the feds.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't use hunters too frequently if the players don't give me reason. But if they are too careless, hunters may even become the main aspect of the game until they manage to loose them again.<br /> <br /> BUT I don't run V5 and don't have the SI in my games. If I ever use it, I'll make it into something very different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T06:01:51-08:00","id":1555018,"title":"","content":"Thanks for taking all that time to redo your post, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>. It's appreciated that you are so invested and I will try to answer everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T07:48:01-08:00","id":1555023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554999#post1554999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote a lot, even more than my normal, then lost everything. Hence giving it two days to cool off and try again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In <i>Revised</i> they're spiritually and philosophically a far cry from their origins, but in the height of their <u>power</u>, <i><b>and that's the point</b></i>. </div> </div> </div>That's not necessarily contradictory. My point was the Sabbat was on a downward spiral from its previous position in terms of managing the Beast and that the Tzimsice and Lasombra were losing control due to how much of the organization was becoming less about being an organized post-human group and more just a bunch of vampire orcs with no Paths to guide them. The Sabbat was a house of cards that by becoming &quot;Camarilla but meaner&quot; was doomed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At this point they're an allegory for a Christian <i>cult</i> (although not perfect), the war on the Ancients is mere propaganda. The Paths, their institutions, their ritae, everything evolved into a form that serves the purposes of their leadership (Elders, by the way), fomenting loyalty and keeping them working. </div> </div> </div>I thought the set up was that wasn't working and the Sabbat was inherently unstable even with the vaulderie, monomancy, and all the other ways that were attempts to keep them focused on the Camarilla violence wise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This corruption of their original state is their degeneration, and the endpoint is power and wealth for their Elders. They still have a lot of what made them the Sabbat in the first place, so they still have a lot to lose, and if they stay in course they'll become just a new flavor of Camarilla. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Sabbat Elders are riding a tiger and were inevitably going to get thrown off. Mind you, you know my biases versus the Anarchs. My opinion regarding the Sabbat was that its Elders were failing to control the Sabbat horde even by Revised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Giving up their extensive secular power and wealth to become a wandering army goes against this to become a straw-man of themselves, above all it misses the point of their allegory and their evolution. It takes the propaganda at face value to become something that isn't either point of the spectrum, but a hollow mockery of itself. </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I think its unintentional but politically accurate to today's times that the true believers are manipulated by cynical political operators eventually overtake the movement. It has to be unintentional because it actually is a good allegory. *rimshot*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One thing must be clear: the Sabbat is not an allegory on terrorism. Vampire is from 1991, cults were a far more pressing matter than terrorism. And, in fact, they still are, although this is only being noticed by people again very recently. They're not <i>Al-Qaeda</i>, they're <i>QAnon</i>. And even for a terrorism group they missed a lot of how terrorists actually work, to make what <i>politicians say</i> terrorist groups are like. </div> </div> </div>This is where I'm going to argue because the Sabbat were depicted as an army first and by the time that V:TM's Old World of Darkness ended in 2004, obviously terrorism was on the mind of just about everyone. Yes, Waco happened in 1993 but that was after Second Edition had firmly established the Sabbat with the Players Guide to the Sabbat. Fundamentally, I think the Sabbat were always designed with vampire lore in mind and providing antagonists as well as enemies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First it's not about how they read scripture, but their attitude about it in the first place. They are Christians, they defend Christianity, they fight what they perceive as enemies of the faith when it comes to it. The worse thing for the Sabbat isn't the Ancients or the Camarilla, it's actually Infernalism, and while there are a number of Infernalists within their ranks they live in secret and fear, because the party line is no mercy, no compromise, no tolerance in any way, shape or form. </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat worship Caine, hate God, loathe the Church as wlel as Christian denominations, and believe that their actions are spiting the god that has damned them. They don't worship the Devil or demons not because they aren't a anti-Christian religion but because demons inevitably get the better of Sabbat in deals. Mind you, I think it's important to also note that the Bishop, Cardinal, Priest, and so on titles are meant to be satirical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, what you call &quot;Satanic&quot;? In the Hebrew bible &quot;\u015b\u0101\u1e6d\u0101n&quot; is actually a title for a role of &quot;prosecutor, opposer&quot;, an entity that either tests or the faithful or argues against them, with Ha-Satan being a title for the angel that mainly holds this role. This is literally what the Sabbat do and do in direct service to YHWH. Actual enemies of YHWH are their enemies too. </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat hate God and want to spite him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whatever you think of their religion and their theology, the point is that they believe in the Christian faith and follow it as they understand it. This is being Christian. </div> </div> </div>Ehhh....<br /> <br /> They don't necessarily believe in Jesus. They believe in Caine. They believe in Noddism but that doesn't necessarily have any new Testament elements. They adopt Catholic trappings and titles out of mockery but they are Abrahamic not Christian. That's assuming the Sabbat aren't atheist or pagan as the religious sects in their ranks include many non-Cainite believers like the Serpents of Light, Veles worship (Slavic pagans), and atheists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not arguing theology and their role within their beliefs, I'm arguing religious identity. They identify as Christians, interpret Christian scripture and dialogue with other Christian groups. This is what being Christian means from a sociological/thematic standpoint. </div> </div> </div>Sabbat don't necessarily believe in Jesus. However, they do believe they are enemies of God and that they will destroy his people so they can rule over him. They're Christians in the same sense the followers of Morgoth in the Lord of the Rings are worshipers of Eru. We're also in &quot;fantasyland&quot; where Hammer Horror vampires are worshipers of Satan and relating too much to &quot;reality&quot; runs risks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire was not that niche. During its heyday it was very famous, if only as the strange game of those goth kids. What made it miss the worse of the Satanic Panic in part of the US is that the Satanic Panic was in the 80s, by the 90s it was starting to cool down, so when Vampire became widely known it was getting the milder version of it. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also it helped that Vampire didn't had demons, not overtly. The Baali would only be mentioned in 1992 in the <i>Storyteller Handbook</i>, but worked for real only starting in 1996 with DA. Demons had far more sway with the Panic than pop-culture legends, even if they were monsters. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I always felt the Sabbat lost something when they de-emphasized the Inquisition and demon worship in the sect. The Path of Evil Revelations was something I felt was a fascinating and interesting story as were the Sabbat who hunted them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First they didn't change it to the point of most vampires being recent Embraces, they run a version where a lot of vampires in a city are still Ancillae, or otherwise older than 2000, as by the start of V5 you can still have Neonates from as early as the 60s. </div> </div> </div>Cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, they re-add Elders almost immediately, because they don't want to really make the setting work differently from what it would otherwise, and that's my problem. For all intents and purposes the demographics changed, but it's never really described as such and it has none of the impact it should have on vampire society, only the vague idea of a power vacuum that isn't ever really that important when it's even real. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's a weird vampire game that doesn't have immortals. It eliminates a huge chunk of the game's themes and ideas as well as the point of being a vampire.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T08:12:31-08:00","id":1555025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And mind you, we start this under the assumption that this organization, no matter how fractured or whatever, just wiped out all vampires of a major city under their command. This is huge, so the idea that this organization can't keep even <i>minimal</i> scrutiny afterwards is hard to believe. And as important as this, the idea that the Camarilla set up shop almost immediately after without any regard for this risk, when this number of vampires coming from the outside at once is already a hard thing to happen. </div> </div> </div>I suppose my point is that I think the Second Inquisition is an overstretched, badly organized, fractured organization in my view versus the opposite. FIRSTLIGHT is an alliance of the Arcanum, SAD, NSA, loose hunter organizations with the Society of Leopold basically calling the shots by being the only people who 100% have an idea of what to do. I suppose I can't imagine that they're not chasing fires and extremely overstretched, especially since every time they show up in video games and canonical storylines, they take heavy casualties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a lot of things besides the lack of vigilance by the SI that must happen in a very specific and unlikely way to justify the Cam societies that formed in those two cities. And while none of them is strictly impossible, it's just A LOT of unlikely events in succession, making it quite contrived with no further explanation. And it happened twice. </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree about that but I also think the games heavily imply the Second Inquisition does a little damage, declares victory, moves out, and then the Camarilla moves in. Primarily because they know the SI can't bother wasting resources there and also because the Sabbat left most of the places with a minimum of remnants anyway because so many went to fight the Gehenna Wars.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe, but it could very well have been from the books, because that's mostly how the Technocracy works in any book that actually describes it. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wish I remembered where that was discussed.<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pentex was silly. It was silly by design, always have been. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think the World of Darkness being silly is something that is to its credit not the opposite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their main narrative role is to play on office-comedy. It's not the <i><b>only</b></i> thing they do, but it's their main shtick. </div> </div> </div>A non-joke that every satire of corporate culture is seemingly less creepy and weird than the reality.<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They were doing that. The whole SPD debacle in the Syndicate was about that. </div> </div> </div>I thought the point of the SPD was the opposite. They didn't want the Syndicate tied to a bunch of Garou Nephandus-style monsters so they had the SPD disappear from the Technocracy Revised. Which was a shame really as I felt that gave a very interesting storyline for Syndicate mages to deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of people in-the-know about vampires and with stakes on their assets could be financing the SI. </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd back down from making this an official thing just because this brings potential changes to the game that won't be for every game. This kind of relationship changes a lot on how the game runs and the themes it brings once this layer of the conspiracy starts to be peeled. A broader and more generic set of bakers may give it the Financial Conspiracy twist without changing that much on the basic assumptions of a regular game. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, despite attempts to make it more crossover friendly, a lot of people think the Technocracy being a thing undermines the themes of V:TM. After all, if the Technocracy and Pentex exists then the Camarilla doesn't rule the world as the undead Illuminati.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Society of Leopold is a group of religious zealots. Their worldview is hyper-focused on the idea of ridding the world of the servants of the Devil as they understand it. They have no interest in understanding broader or more complex social matters, only the interests of the Church as <u>they</u> understand them. Having rich benefactors is par of the course for such groups, and fighting pagans and heretics is well within their purview. They are, by design, ultimately incapable of discerning their real enemies. </div> </div> </div>The Society of Leopold is depicted as calling the shots of the Second Inquisition but I don't think this is something that is going to last in the setting's metaplot. Basically, the SI has a very clear mission statement: wipe out the undead when the early groups became aware. Which I suspect provided the organization a lot of its early direction but once the governments of the world are better informed, they will gradually move from the Society's influence.<br /> <br /> That's just how I think they're presented. The NSA doesn't even like using religious terms, hence blank bodies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the Arcanum ultimately isn't neither invested in a particular stance nor privy to every supernatural secret in the world. They don't know about Pentex, and are unlikely to care beyond curiosity about their supernatural ties if they find out. They don't really know enough to recognize the Wyrm or its tools, this is not their thing. And things get worse with a version of the Arcane that's in the SI, which goes against the organization as previously thought. This Arcane is even less likley to know anything about spiritual corruption of any kind.\u200b </div> </div> </div>FYI, AMC has reimagined the Talamasca (Arcanum's inspiration) as a bunch of spies rather than academics. I find that depressing and hilarious.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T15:45:08-08:00","id":1555075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555023#post1555023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not necessarily contradictory. My point was the Sabbat was on a downward spiral from its previous position in terms of managing the Beast and that the Tzimsice and Lasombra were losing control due to how much of the organization was becoming less about being an organized post-human group and more just a bunch of vampire orcs with no Paths to guide them. The Sabbat was a house of cards that by becoming &quot;Camarilla but meaner&quot; was doomed.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's something to this, but is more complex. And again, one of the problems with how V5 did it is that it simply striped the Sabbat from its complexity, and <u>that</u> was not what they were heading to.<br /> <br /> First things first: <i>Revised</i> was in many ways a proto-V5 in the way it tried to steer the game towards a more specific and closed vision of how it should be, and the idea of the Sabbat as loosing control was pretty much a part of this. So there is some important nuance between the Sabbat of each edition, not only from pre-V5 to V5. Most of what you described was <i>Revised</i> Sabbat and no other version of it, for whatever it's worth.<br /> <br /> But even then, and admitting they're a more complex and bigger society than even I argued (I stand by my previous arguments, but want to add they're far from the full picture of the Sabbat), the Sabbat is not on <b>this</b> kind of downward spiral. <i>Revised</i> made the Paths less universal as a retcon, to begin with, not a movement. And while control of the Sabbat on a societal frame was at peril, that had nothing to do with personal self-control against the Beast.<br /> <br /> And the Sabbat as an army doesn't actually continues such a trend even if it was real. It's not about the Beast winning or the clans loosing their grip, it's actually about the Paths becoming even more effective and social control becoming tighter than ever. A degenerate Sabbat in this sense would be overtaken by Wassail and virtually impossible to organize in anything bigger than a pack with half a dozen members. Instead we have everyone on Paths, no apparent signs of anyone falling to the Beast with any regularity, and the whole thing organized into an actual army.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555023#post1555023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, I think its unintentional but politically accurate to today's times that the true believers are manipulated by cynical political operators eventually overtake the movement. It has to be unintentional because it actually is a good allegory. *rimshot*</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where you get this idea.<br /> <br /> When extremists overtake the movement it isn't because they grow out of control, it is because an even more cynical operator takes their reins from those who want to compromise in the name of &quot;normalcy&quot;.<br /> <br /> But the Sabbat is, in certain ways, going the opposite way in <i>Revised</i>. It has been under extremist control for a long time, but now it's getting hard for those guys to control because it's growing too complex and nuanced, with ever more members that don't follow the party creed, even if they follow their rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555023#post1555023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is where I'm going to argue because the Sabbat were depicted as an army first and by the time that V:TM's Old World of Darkness ended in 2004, obviously terrorism was on the mind of just about everyone. Yes, Waco happened in 1993 but that was after Second Edition had firmly established the Sabbat with the Players Guide to the Sabbat. Fundamentally, I think the Sabbat were always designed with vampire lore in mind and providing antagonists as well as enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrorists are not armies. States have armies. The reason why some state-like actors get called &quot;terrorists&quot; is political, not technical.<br /> <br /> It is part and parcel of how terrorists as an actual phenomenon operate that they don't have a proper army or anything like that. They're distinct from guerrillas, governing bodies (aspiring or not) or organized societies. All those can make heavy use of wanton violence and terror tactics, but they're not the same thing. As a quick fact, some groups are called &quot;terrorists&quot; precisely as a means to deny them recognition as anything else and justify the use of anti-terrorist tools when they're less efficient, but politically more interesting. As they say, &quot;don't negotiate with terrorists&quot;.<br /> <br /> So cults can have standing armies when they're big enough, and some historically had. The LDS Church, for example, fought a number of local armed conflicts before settling in Utah, and they were a cult at the time and for quite some time.<br /> <br /> But you're right that, ultimately, the Sabbat is more about a role in Vampire than being specifically an allegory. Yet, this only means they have more nuance, not that they're not a cult, or that they're actually terrorists. As someone who claims domain over territory and has a standing army, by definition they're not terrorists.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555023#post1555023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat worship Caine, hate God, loathe the Church as wlel as Christian denominations, and believe that their actions are spiting the god that has damned them. They don't worship the Devil or demons not because they aren't a anti-Christian religion but because demons inevitably get the better of Sabbat in deals. Mind you, I think it's important to also note that the Bishop, Cardinal, Priest, and so on titles are meant to be satirical.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where you got this info, because as I read the books, that's not what I see.<br /> <br /> While young members frequently use symbols like crucifixes as ironic affectation, the older members get annoyed at this precisely because they think it blasphemous to do so without believing. The titles are <b>not</b> satirical, even if not completely equivalent to the Church. They certainly don't think of themselves as part of the Catholic Church (except those who are), but they're pretty serious as far as the leadership goes (specially <b>Lasombra</b>) on being Christians.<br /> <br /> They're linked to the old Cainite Heresy, they think about Caine as a holy figure, not an enemy of YHWH. Even if they don't think of Caine as the first Messiah (and some do), they do believe in Jesus as the Messiah and they do believe themselves as YHWH servants.<br /> <br /> Even if there's possible non-Christian readings of the Book of Nod (and if you know anything about the other Abrahamic faiths, you know a lot of the Book of Nod is specifically Christian, even if it isn't nominally New Testament), the Sabbat specifically does a Christian reading of it.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear: Judaism and Islam are not simply Christanity <i>sans</i> New Testament. There's a lot of differences in theology beyond that that applies even to the other scripture, and also other texts beyond just the Christian Old Testament. Islam doesn't even deny the NT, it's scripture to them, and Jesus is a prophet. Don't try to argue something is &quot;non-Christian Abrahamic&quot; just because it's Old Testament, if it is a reading of it familiar to Christians, it's pretty much Christianity.<br /> <br /> Also, their hunting of Infernalism definitely goes far beyond just thinking demons get the better of them. They have an Inquisition precisely because of how important hunting demons is to them beyond just thinking it's a bad idea. They are not satanic vampires, although they have some trappings of this trope.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555023#post1555023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's assuming the Sabbat aren't atheist or pagan as the religious sects in their ranks include many non-Cainite believers like the Serpents of Light, Veles worship (Slavic pagans), and atheists.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the many peculiar Sabbat characteristics is that it's open to many faiths even if they're not the party's official one, as long as you don't openly deny Caine.<br /> <br /> So yes, there are many other faiths in the Sabbat. It just doesn't change what the party line is.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555023#post1555023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's a weird vampire game that doesn't have immortals. It eliminates a huge chunk of the game's themes and ideas as well as the point of being a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you can't have a game where most vampires are new because shit is hitting the fan, yet most vampires are old because you want a regular vampire game.<br /> <br /> This is the whole point of not committing to their changes to the setting, those changes <b>do</b> make for a weird vampire game, which isn't necessarily a bad one. But they wanted to make the changes and yet ignore their impacts, so they can have a &quot;normal&quot; vampire game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555025#post1555025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose my point is that I think the Second Inquisition is an overstretched, badly organized, fractured organization in my view versus the opposite. FIRSTLIGHT is an alliance of the Arcanum, SAD, NSA, loose hunter organizations with the Society of Leopold basically calling the shots by being the only people who 100% have an idea of what to do. I suppose I can't imagine that they're not chasing fires and extremely overstretched, especially since every time they show up in video games and canonical storylines, they take heavy casualties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's not the SI of the books, specially the early ones.<br /> <br /> I'll say again, we're specifically talking the organization that just wiped out vampires in those cities. Whatever we think of them, we have to start from this point, and it's not related as something that happened because they were leaving anyway. However stretched or fractured this organization is, at this point in time it managed to do quite an impressive job, especially considering that they did so in two big cities without making them into war zones or breaking the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> However Americans usually think violent foreign cities are, Ciudad de M\u00e9xico is the biggest city in North America in population (yes, bigger than NY) and an economic powerhouse. Fighting a hidden enemy in there isn't any easier than doing it in any big US city. It isn't a frontier scenario, it doesn't have biker gangs running around like they own the whole place, it won't just ignore a paramilitary group doing whatever they want within it. Things don't get much different in Montreal, except it's safer.<br /> <br /> And the problem, again, is that keeping vigilance requires <i><b>WAY</b></i> less resources than this, and is in the ballpark of what the SI does <i>according to the books</i>. Even if this is not your SI, it is the SI in the books. And more importantly, the Camarilla doesn't have the means to know all that even if it's true. It's a fantastically weird movement for the Cam to move in so soon after the cleansing as they <b>don't know</b> if the thing that did it so thoroughly is still there in some way, and it isn't hard for them to be.<br /> <br /> The problem isn't just what the SI can <i>actually</i> do, but that the Camarilla assuming they can't do much was an incredibly stupid move, unless they had <b><i>a lot</i></b> of inside info the books don't give any reason to think they have. And then we have the whole logistics of moving an entire population of vampires from elsewhere, the problem of <i>finding</i> those interested parties in the first place, the work to make them into a functional Cam society that doesn't look like it was founded yesterday...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555025#post1555025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't disagree about that but I also think the games heavily imply the Second Inquisition does a little damage, declares victory, moves out, and then the Camarilla moves in. Primarily because they know the SI can't bother wasting resources there and also because the Sabbat left most of the places with a minimum of remnants anyway because so many went to fight the Gehenna Wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they don't.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this isn't an ok headcanon to run the game, but that's not what's in the actual books.<br /> <br /> The SI victories, at least <i>at the time of those cities' intervention</i>, are described as quite impressive and, most important, <i>surprising to the Camarilla</i>.<br /> <br /> Yes, a lot of inside work and other shenanigans may have helped the SI to do this stuff. <b>But that's not what the books say</b>, and definitely isn't what the Camarilla knew. The Camarilla knew nothing, and should expect the worse out of safety, <b>which is what they did according to the books</b>, except for taking those cities pronto for some reason.<br /> <br /> Of course you can easily say that most of the news were overblown by that time without technically changing the setting, but saying the books imply any of this is reading in them what you want to have as a headcanon. They don't. And even if they did, the Camarilla didn't knew at the time, so the Cam acting like it know for sure when the SI stops being a threat is profoundly stupid. And yes, <i>some</i> people in the Cam may know in your game. But we're talking <i><b>a lot</b></i> of people moving in.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555025#post1555025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I think the World of Darkness being silly is something that is to its credit not the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Just pointing out that Pentex was done like that by design.<br /> <br /> To be precise, Pentex is an open joke. The most open joke in the WoD, probably. It's dark comedy, not horror, and has never been intended as anything else.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has a very different tone from Vampire, so this kind of open comedy flies there without breaking immersion as much as it would in VtM, even in Pentex' scale.<br /> <br /> People who don't like comedy in their game should stop complaining about Pentex as it is in the books and just not use it (as it is in the books).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555025#post1555025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A non-joke that every satire of corporate culture is seemingly less creepy and weird than the reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I live this reality now, I know how it is...<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555025#post1555025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the point of the SPD was the opposite. They didn't want the Syndicate tied to a bunch of Garou Nephandus-style monsters so they had the SPD disappear from the Technocracy Revised. Which was a shame really as I felt that gave a very interesting storyline for Syndicate mages to deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was the case they would just have the SPD be turned into an example, not a whole new plot.<br /> <br /> What they did was to effectively give Agents, especially Syndicate ones, an entirely new avenue for stories about Pentex and the Wyrm, with the possibility of heavy crossover with Werewolves and other Fera.<br /> <br /> Their presence in Mage stopped being just a nod to become an integral part of their current metaplot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555025#post1555025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, despite attempts to make it more crossover friendly, a lot of people think the Technocracy being a thing undermines the themes of V:TM. After all, if the Technocracy and Pentex exists then the Camarilla doesn't rule the world as the undead Illuminati.</div> </div> </div> </div>They change the game. This isn't by itself good or bad, but they change the game. The classical themes and mood of Vampire don't survive a full crossover, giving way to new themes and mood. Those can still be ok, but they're just not the same.<br /> <br /> So full crossover really has never been an option. The game simply wasn't built for this, not without giving up a lot of what people want out of it. And this isn't true only for Vampire, although it was worse for Vampire as it was made literally without any passing consideration or awareness of the other games.<br /> <br /> Even then, the same goes for every other gameline. If you crossover Vampire and Mage, you're also saying the Union never had all that control over how humanity was evolving because a lot of things that happened were secretly vampire schemes. If you fully integrate VtM in a Mage game, there are vampire lackeys infiltrated everywhere, including Mages, and most of the conspiracies going on are actually unrelated to the Union.<br /> <br /> Again, this changes the game considerably, it changes mood, themes, assumptions. It may make for a fun game, nonetheless, but it simply isn't the classic feeling.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555025#post1555025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Society of Leopold is depicted as calling the shots of the Second Inquisition but I don't think this is something that is going to last in the setting's metaplot. Basically, the SI has a very clear mission statement: wipe out the undead when the early groups became aware. Which I suspect provided the organization a lot of its early direction but once the governments of the world are better informed, they will gradually move from the Society's influence.<br /> <br /> That's just how I think they're presented. The NSA doesn't even like using religious terms, hence blank bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another problem I see with your depiction is that you conflate the lack of <i>unified</i> efficiency with a lack of efficiency whatsoever.<br /> <br /> However stretched and fragmentary the SI may be, it's still composed of independently functional parts. It doesn't need every piece to work together to get things done, a lot can be made by those parts on their own. Setting up vigilance is one of the things that a lot of SI components can do by themselves. In fact, if they're starting to distrust each other, they may very well do so all at once, each keeping their own &quot;watchtower&quot;.<br /> <br /> What makes the SI work is them knowing each other, being willing to share info on enemies, at least the presence of targets, and all of them wanting to hunt vampires. Coordination is secondary to them being dangerous, even if it makes them far more dangerous. Yes, they need coordination to bomb Vienna, but keeping vigilance in an already cleansed city isn't bombing Vienna.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555025#post1555025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FYI, AMC has reimagined the Talamasca (Arcanum's inspiration) as a bunch of spies rather than academics. I find that depressing and hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T17:45:41-08:00","id":1555084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555025#post1555025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, despite attempts to make it more crossover friendly, a lot of people think the Technocracy being a thing undermines the themes of V:TM. After all, if the Technocracy and Pentex exists then the Camarilla doesn't rule the world as the undead Illuminati.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Second Inquisition, in and of itself, demonstrates that the Camarilla doesn't rule the world and that there is a higher level conspiracy between governments that vampires don't have really have control over or much access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T22:25:35-08:00","id":1555091,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <br /> <br /> To address most of what you brought up at once rather than individually, for which I'm sure we'll both be grateful (tehehe), I think the Second Inquisition has a disjointed depiction that you bring up a lot of things that are perfectly valid for regarding its resources. Yes, the SI is depicted as having successfully cleansed the Sabbat in Montreal, Mexico City, Camarilla in London, Vienna, almost did the same in Boston, may or may not have done so in Las Vegas, and has launched attacks in many other cities. Aside from The Fall of London, none of these have also been shown to be the Camarilla misusing them and Mithras is the only real case of, &quot;the SI was an inside job&quot; we know to be true.<br /> <br /> We do know the Camarilla did screw up by attempting to use the SI against the Anarchs and that helped expose them. However, we don't know the extent of this and how successful or unsuccessful it was until it backfired. A lot of this is from THE CAMARILLA's SI section that I feel like should have been in the SI book instead.<br /> <br /> However, this is where the part gets confusing because the Camarilla doesn't actually act like it's on the backfoot. Yes, they've banned cell phones and are now communicating between hand-written letters and messengers (possibly even crows because Animalism and Game of Thrones) but the Camarilla is still doing all the same stuff they used to. Elysiums, courts, and large international global politics. They aren't panicking (even with the rise of the Anarch Movement as a full-on legitimate sect with three clans). Hell, they're even using graffiti tags of their symbols now. I wonder if the Camarilla is meant to be stupid or if the SI doesn't pose the threat people think it does in-canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T23:36:03-08:00","id":1555096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555091#post1555091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the Camarilla is meant to be stupid or if the SI doesn't pose the threat people think it does in-canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're kind of going extremes here, they're either completely feared or pose no threat.<br /> <br /> Even putting aside that Paradox don't commit to changes in the setting, so the Camarilla acting normal isn't unexpected, the fact remains that the SI may be a threat and still not impede the Cam from doing their stuff in territories the SI didn't burn to the ground (metaphorically). You acknowledge yourself that the SI had a lot of successes in the books and can completely cleanse entire cities from vampires, including big Camarilla cities, and they pressed the Camarilla into avoiding tech they previously relied a lot upon.<br /> <br /> So yeah, they're not overbearing enough for the Cam to be in full panic mode, at least not anymore, but that doesn't mean they're not dangerous. That's like saying rabies is the only dangerous viral disease, as it's the only one with 100% mortality rate. I'm not arguing the SI in any and every situation or city, I'm talking the SI specifically in the two Sabbat cities it cleansed. Just because the Cam isn't panicking everywhere else doesn't mean they shouldn't be careful in those cities, where the SI had recently enough of a presence to dig up every single vampire resident.<br /> <br /> The problem I'm pointing here isn't if the Cam fears the SI or not, or how much of a threat the SI is. Those things are actually inconsistent through the books. I'm talking how little sense it makes for them to have a full regular Cam domain in those two cities, and the actual SI resources is only a small aspect of it. Simply finding enough vampires elsewhere to fill those cities is a challenge, and moving them is yet another. We're talking the vampiric equivalent of a mass migration, from many, many places, and frequently through hostile territory, while trying to not attract attention. All that to form a society that looks like it has always been there.<br /> <br /> And in the end that's the problem: they wanted those cities to feel like regular Cam territory, as if they've always been Camarilla territory, and doing it through SI intervention is stupid, because the SI intervention calls for a lot of considerations and a story of how it happened that they don't want to make or tell, they just skipped it and made the place work as if nothing exceptional happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T11:03:05-08:00","id":1555129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1554867#post1554867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but that's a discussion-killing argument.<br /> <br /> We all know we can ignore the books and do whatever. Many of us have plenty of experience doing so.<br /> <br /> But discussing the setting means discussing what's officially in the books, because that's the common ground we have. Otherwise it's completely pointless.<br /> <br /> <br /> I personally think the books did showed this previously.<br /> <br /> Since 1st edition, all a mortal needs to be a big, real problem is to know enough about you and be about during the day. A mortal can literally bulldoze your Haven. Bring a flamethrower to a fight. Use assault rifles and hand grenades.<br /> <br /> Technology is more powerful than Disciplines, hands down. In the Middle Ages you could have a stone castle and be pretty safe against mortals even if they knew about you, nowadays that's far from enough.<br /> <br /> Classic VtM is about vampires living as the secret masters of the world, that ultimately must remain secret because collective Humanity is just too dangerous. By the way, the Technocracy does not have nearly enough nukes to eliminate every Ante, <u><b>but Russia and the US have</b></u>. Direct domination simply isn't an option. And hunters have always existed, plenty of them, all with the resources to make things hard for vampire even if they can't hope to survive a direct confrontation with an Elder.<br /> <br /> What the SI does is to increase the background danger to a degree where vampires aren't even in control anymore, as the SI is the one in control of military assets around the world.<br /> <br /> You can add nuance to this? Surely. Is it simple and homogeneous? Definitely not. But it is a fundamentally distinct premise for the game, even if they're now mostly ignoring it because they want to pretend this is Classic VtM.<br /> <br /> And I personally find that the biggest problem with the SI (and with most setting changes from the beginning of V5) isn't that it exists, but that Paradox wanted to make big moves, but not commit to them.<br /> <br /> V5 shouldn't try to be Masquerade as usual, it should thoroughly embrace its own identity.</div> </div> </div> </div> I suspect a key element of the problem is that writers too often think in terms of Epochal change, rather than in Eras: they assume their changes will create THE Status Quo, rather than a new status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T14:02:03-08:00","id":1555135,"title":"","content":"Its also quite odd that the carmarilla is moving into cleansed or abandoned sabbat territories. The more obvious group would be anarchs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T15:00:00-08:00","id":1555136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555096#post1555096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're kind of going extremes here, they're either completely feared or pose no threat.<br /> <br /> Even putting aside that Paradox don't commit to changes in the setting, so the Camarilla acting normal isn't unexpected, the fact remains that the SI may be a threat and still not impede the Cam from doing their stuff in territories the SI didn't burn to the ground (metaphorically). You acknowledge yourself that the SI had a lot of successes in the books and can completely cleanse entire cities from vampires, including big Camarilla cities, and they pressed the Camarilla into avoiding tech they previously relied a lot upon.<br /> <br /> So yeah, they're not overbearing enough for the Cam to be in full panic mode, at least not anymore, but that doesn't mean they're not dangerous. That's like saying rabies is the only dangerous viral disease, as it's the only one with 100% mortality rate. I'm not arguing the SI in any and every situation or city, I'm talking the SI specifically in the two Sabbat cities it cleansed. Just because the Cam isn't panicking everywhere else doesn't mean they shouldn't be careful in those cities, where the SI had recently enough of a presence to dig up every single vampire resident.<br /> <br /> The problem I'm pointing here isn't if the Cam fears the SI or not, or how much of a threat the SI is. Those things are actually inconsistent through the books. I'm talking how little sense it makes for them to have a full regular Cam domain in those two cities, and the actual SI resources is only a small aspect of it. Simply finding enough vampires elsewhere to fill those cities is a challenge, and moving them is yet another. We're talking the vampiric equivalent of a mass migration, from many, many places, and frequently through hostile territory, while trying to not attract attention. All that to form a society that looks like it has always been there.<br /> <br /> And in the end that's the problem: they wanted those cities to feel like regular Cam territory, as if they've always been Camarilla territory, and doing it through SI intervention is stupid, because the SI intervention calls for a lot of considerations and a story of how it happened that they don't want to make or tell, they just skipped it and made the place work as if nothing exceptional happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have an issue with the idea that there's a &quot;Gold Rush&quot; when it comes to cities that have been depopulated by the Second Inquisition or Sabbat abandoning of large chunks of their former territory. One of the chief consistent parts of V:TM is the idea that the Anarch vs. Camarilla conflict is primarily due to the competition over land (domain) as well as siring rights.<br /> <br /> I don't think the transportation between cities is nearly as difficult as a lot of people suggest it is as well. It's possible to cross the majority of the United States in an evening by car after all and most of these undead have travelled far worse. Certainly, the Camarilla is also a place that would attempt to set its flag down wherever they could.<br /> <br /> I admit, I'm going to believe that a lot of what appears to be consistent storytelling is probably serendipity rather than deliberate design. There have been a lot of upheavals behind the scenes after all but I do think that it fits perfectly into why the Anarchs have gone from being a no-nothing Camarilla faction (in both senses of the word) to being a rival sect that replaced the Sabbat. Not only do they have three Clans as members now but they do have the opportunity to take over portions of all the Sabbat's former cities.<br /> <br /> (Berlin being the new Anarch HQ in Europe does fit my love of Shadowrun, though)<br /> <br /> Again, probably due to serendipity versus planning, it does go a long way to explaining the rise of much younger vampires into positions of power. There is a &quot;New Money&quot; with regards to domains as Hazel Iverson, Kevin Jackson, and other figures show as Ancilla seize princedoms whenever possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T15:59:45-08:00","id":1555141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555136#post1555136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have an issue with the idea that there's a &quot;Gold Rush&quot; when it comes to cities that have been depopulated by the Second Inquisition or Sabbat abandoning of large chunks of their former territory. One of the chief consistent parts of V:TM is the idea that the Anarch vs. Camarilla conflict is primarily due to the competition over land (domain) as well as siring rights.<br /> <br /> I don't think the transportation between cities is nearly as difficult as a lot of people suggest it is as well. It's possible to cross the majority of the United States in an evening by car after all and most of these undead have travelled far worse. Certainly, the Camarilla is also a place that would attempt to set its flag down wherever they could.<br /> <br /> I admit, I'm going to believe that a lot of what appears to be consistent storytelling is probably serendipity rather than deliberate design. There have been a lot of upheavals behind the scenes after all but I do think that it fits perfectly into why the Anarchs have gone from being a no-nothing Camarilla faction (in both senses of the word) to being a rival sect that replaced the Sabbat. Not only do they have three Clans as members now but they do have the opportunity to take over portions of all the Sabbat's former cities.<br /> <br /> (Berlin being the new Anarch HQ in Europe does fit my love of Shadowrun, though)<br /> <br /> Again, probably due to serendipity versus planning, it does go a long way to explaining the rise of much younger vampires into positions of power. There is a &quot;New Money&quot; with regards to domains as Hazel Iverson, Kevin Jackson, and other figures show as Ancilla seize princedoms whenever possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>A &quot;Gold Rush&quot; isn't a bad idea if there's a story behind it that takes into account both all the things that must happen and how distinct is the end result. The way it was done it's not a Gold Rush, it's a couple cities that simply don't make sense.<br /> <br /> It could have a consideration for how risky it was to take the city right away, and how they did to make it safely. It could have an actual plan, or even a mystery, on how the Cam did it so boldly. It could and should be a city colored by the fact it was recently established, the inhabitants are mostly from elsewhere and most power structures are still in flux as they learn about each other while keeping their own secrets from each other, as they didn't had yet time to acclimate for real.<br /> <br /> There's no story, not even a &quot;Gold Rush&quot; story.<br /> <br /> You can't cross most of the US by car in an evening, by the way. It takes 40 to 50 hours of travel by car to cross it coast to coast, that's a lot of evenings. Here's again the matter of nuance and scale, traveling isn't all that hard for a vampire that does their homework, but it isn't something a vampire does without care, either, there are many potential risks. And we're talking dozens of vampires for Montreal and more than two hundred for Ciudad de M\u00e9xico even at conservative numbers. At that scale, even a 1% chance becomes a frequency instead.<br /> <br /> So there's a lot of stories that could and should be told with this endeavor. In fact the &quot;Gold Rush&quot; is a very good analogy for the kind of story you tell with those movements and the kind of cities you have at first (at least from the perspective of vampires). The problem, then, is those stories not existing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T18:08:12-08:00","id":1555145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555136#post1555136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have an issue with the idea that there's a &quot;Gold Rush&quot; when it comes to cities that have been depopulated by the Second Inquisition or Sabbat abandoning of large chunks of their former territory. One of the chief consistent parts of V:TM is the idea that the Anarch vs. Camarilla conflict is primarily due to the competition over land (domain) as well as siring rights.<br /> <br /> I don't think the transportation between cities is nearly as difficult as a lot of people suggest it is as well. It's possible to cross the majority of the United States in an evening by car after all</div> </div> </div> </div>...Are you a wizard of the Time Sphere? Are your evenings actually 15-18 hours long?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T18:29:42-08:00","id":1555148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555145#post1555145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Are you a wizard of the Time Sphere? Are your evenings actually 15-18 hours long?</div> </div> </div> </div>The most boring job in the universe is editing your own manuscript after the edits have come back. So that's when I do a lot of posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T13:06:09-08:00","id":1555172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555148#post1555148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The most boring job in the universe is editing your own manuscript after the edits have come back. So that's when I do a lot of posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T04:40:34-08:00","id":1555232,"title":"","content":"A new ST i introduced to VTM is ST ing a game in vienna where the gold rush is going on. The fresh smell has rubbed of pretty quickly. The convo we had was like this:<br /> <br /> Q &quot;Why are all these randoms sent to Vienna? Is this a suicide squat?&quot;<br /> A &quot;Maybe they are there for recon.&quot;<br /> Q &quot;If they are there for recon, why not sent people that are actually good at that? Like Gangrel or Nosferatum, why sent bougie fledgelings? Big red lights going off over my head.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then everything turned into a fairly standard VTM game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T18:52:32-08:00","id":1555254,"title":"","content":"I've always thought that the purpose of the SI was to make VTM extremely small, more like Interview With the Vampire than a story about vampire nation-states at war. The idea was to break the large-scale vampire governments, and make the story very intimately about you, your sire, your human family/friends, and a couple of young vampires turned around the same time. <br /> <br /> They wanted you to live very quietly, and the drama comes from your attempts to balance survival with not exploiting your friends and family too much. Very low-power, very dark and broody, very tiny. <br /> <br /> The SI were made so powerful to almost completely stop violence as the solution. Violence is something that happens rarely, probably because of a failed roll, and then you struggle to cover it up using powers that are little more than parlor-tricks. <br /> <br /> In short, they wanted to make your story tiny, by making the enemy so big that you had to be utterly devoted to quietly, quietly, quietly hiding from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T19:08:38-08:00","id":1555256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555254#post1555254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought that the purpose of the SI was to make VTM extremely small, more like Interview With the Vampire than a story about vampire nation-states at war. The idea was to break the large-scale vampire governments, and make the story very intimately about you, your sire, your human family/friends, and a couple of young vampires turned around the same time.<br /> <br /> They wanted you to live very quietly, and the drama comes from your attempts to balance survival with not exploiting your friends and family too much. Very low-power, very dark and broody, very tiny.<br /> <br /> The SI were made so powerful to almost completely stop violence as the solution. Violence is something that happens rarely, probably because of a failed roll, and then you struggle to cover it up using powers that are little more than parlor-tricks.<br /> <br /> In short, they wanted to make your story tiny, by making the enemy so big that you had to be utterly devoted to quietly, quietly, quietly hiding from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, the Camarilla is larger than its ever been before with it now merged with the Ashirra and the Kuei-Jin seemingly vanished from the face of the Earth (and nothing of value was lost).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T19:17:31-08:00","id":1555258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555256#post1555256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, the Camarilla is larger than its ever been before with it now merged with the Ashirra and the Kuei-Jin seemingly vanished from the face of the Earth (and nothing of value was lost).</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they are inconsistent and don't commit to what they do, and also the Camarilla isn't larger than ever because it expelled most of its lower tiers to become a private club.<br /> <br /> And a lot of people like KotE, some even more than VtM, so I'd say definitely something of value was lost. Just because it was a badly thought response to an actual need that didn't really solve that need, it doesn't means it wasn't a good thing to exist that could be repurposed so its fans aren't just ignored and abandoned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T19:21:37-08:00","id":1555259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555258#post1555258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they are inconsistent and don't commit to what they do, and also the Camarilla isn't larger than ever because it expelled most of its lower tiers to become a private club.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expelled the Brujah (except plenty remained) and Gangrel (ditto) but gained the Banu Haqim and Lasombra.<br /> <br /> But yes, I don't think the Second Inquisition was ever intended to make the Camarilla smaller as it seems more global than it ever was before. I think it was just meant to provide more antagonists and keep the tech level low.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And a lot of people like KotE, some even more than VtM, so I'd say definitely something of value was lost. Just because it was a badly thought response to an actual need that didn't really solve that need, it doesn't means it wasn't a good thing to exist that could be repurposed so its fans aren't just ignored and abandoned. </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I'd rather be a voice of positivity than negativity anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T03:38:15-08:00","id":1555264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555258#post1555258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they are inconsistent and don't commit to what they do, and also the Camarilla isn't larger than ever because it expelled most of its lower tiers to become a private club.<br /> <br /> And a lot of people like KotE, some even more than VtM, so I'd say definitely something of value was lost. Just because it was a badly thought response to an actual need that didn't really solve that need, it doesn't means it wasn't a good thing to exist that could be repurposed so its fans aren't just ignored and abandoned.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is kinda weird in how it approaches the tower. On one hand it seems to want to be a 1% gated community/old boys club/dinner party from hell. On the other hand its absurdly warcraft style global and has more clans/groups with formal membership than any other sect. <br /> <br /> Yeah koe needs a rewrite and a lot of spit and polish rather than w5 treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-09-2025, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T08:42:35-08:00","id":1555267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/15547