]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T09:01:35-08:00","id":1555269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555268#post1555268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose this means that Ming Xiao is Tzimisce or the local equivalent now.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 still could be an alternate timeline<br /> Frankly considering they dragged back before confirmed dead characters who pulled a Palpatine and somehow returned...?<br /> It even would make sense than, yeah, Ming Xiao was a Tzimsice or the local equivalent... prlase ignore the man behind the courtian and the fact she called herself a Kuei Jin and had a Yama King deep discussion with a Malkavian","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T09:05:11-08:00","id":1555270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555269#post1555269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 still could be an alternate timeline<br /> Frankly considering they dragged back before confirmed dead characters who pulled a Palpatine and somehow returned...?<br /> It even would make sense than, yeah, Ming Xiao was a Tzimsice or the local equivalent... prlase ignore the man behind the courtian and the fact she called herself a Kuei Jin and had a Yama King deep discussion with a Malkavian</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh you fell for that propaganda?<br /> <br /> I mean Kuei Jin doesn't even make sense linguistically!<br /> <br /> Misinformation, my friend. The local Chinese Tzimisce are hiding their connection to the Eldest.<br /> <br /> - Malkavian Fledgling","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T12:00:18-08:00","id":1555277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555270#post1555270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean Kuei Jin doesn't even make sense linguistically!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Neither does caine.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T12:37:20-08:00","id":1555280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555259#post1555259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expelled the Brujah (except plenty remained) and Gangrel (ditto) but gained the Banu Haqim and Lasombra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about individuals, not clans, and how the Cam became an Old Boys Club instead of accepting everyone by default.<br /> <br /> Outside the most obnoxious reading of clan roles, I don't know how you understood I was talking about clan representation in the Inner Circle.<br /> <br /> And the Camarilla already was as global as it gets, the main difference now is how the game seems to be <i><u>retroactively</u></i> making Asia and Africa part of the known vampire community, but as a retcon it means this applies to the old Cam as well, the Ashirra answers only for the Middle East. This is not exactly the Camarille becoming bigger, but the game becoming simpler.<br /> <br /> Which isn't necessarily a bad thing by itself. While I have my criticism of their take, it's not the point. My point is just that the SI didn't caused or let the Camarilla grow, first because the Camarilla didn't grew in the lore and second because it has more to do with the writers not giving the SI its full logical effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555268#post1555268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer a more universal V:TM with the Clans but that was an incredibly harsh response from Paradox.<br /> <br /> I think they did fantastic work reworking the Ravnos and Banu Haqim.<br /> <br /> I suppose this means that Ming Xiao is Tzimisce or the local equivalent now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Late <i>Second Edition</i> did a fantastic work with the Ravnos and <i>Revised</i> did a fantastic work with the Banu Haqim, most of what V5 does with both is a direct continuation of previous work.<br /> <br /> Also, it remains that KotE sets the start of the War of Shame, which is central to a lot of the setting in the East for everyone.<br /> <br /> Which is interesting, as one of the things they did well with the &quot;Asian Setting&quot; in cWoD is that they really made a unified setting there.<br /> <br /> It remains that yeah, a more universal V:tM game was badly needed, but it didn't had to come at the cost of so many past things being simply trashed, no questions asked.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555269#post1555269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">prlase ignore the man behind the courtian and the fact she called herself a Kuei Jin and had a Yama King deep discussion with a Malkavian</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to ignore their lore even if they make her a Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> There's zero need or sense for every old vampire to be a Noddist.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555270#post1555270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean Kuei Jin doesn't even make sense linguistically!</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there many terms in the setting that do?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T13:30:00-08:00","id":1555284,"title":"","content":"I tend to frown upon the western pop cultue style of vampire being universal and dominant ( although them being everywere kinda makes sense from the early modern period) but i find the idea everyone everywhere mimicking the carmarilla/ anarch status every stretches credability, slightly problamatic and frankly, boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T14:16:31-08:00","id":1555285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555284#post1555284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to frown upon the western pop cultue style of vampire being universal and dominant ( although them being everywere kinda makes sense from the early modern period) but i find the idea everyone everywhere mimicking the carmarilla/ anarch status every stretches credability, slightly problamatic and frankly, boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with the Kuei Jin mostly steams from friends in Hong Kong who had strong opinions on the subject. Effectively, their opinion colored mine which was that if someone wants to play Vampire: The Masquerade then they come into the game with the expectation of playing Western vampires or Tremere. Their issues with the game was essentially having their homelands and people kicked out of the cool kids club.<br /> <br /> But I am admonished. No one should regulate anyone's fun, IMHO.<br /> <br /> I think I was also influenced by Chicago by Night 1st Edition too. Part of the fun of that book when I was a very isolated white kid from the South was that it was an incredibly diverse collection of vampires from Vietnam, Greece, France, black, white, and otherwise. The Camarilla felt universe and a large tent that gradually got smaller and smaller as the story progressed. It's especially noticeable when we're dealing with the modern V:TM fandom that are more often than not in nations other than the United States.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if there's an actual answer that pleases everyone and I certainly don't have it. <br /> <br /> But back to the Second Inquisition, I think its interesting to talk about how they've expanded as a concept from V:TM. Hunter.org making it clear that the Entity is an antagonist organization even to other Hunters and clearly depicted as a force for evil. It was oddly my favorite element about 5th Edition Hunter: The Reckoning (I was annoyed they didn't give an optional Imbued template).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-09-2025, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T14:59:12-08:00","id":1555289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555270#post1555270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I prefer a more universal V:TM with the Clans but that was an incredibly harsh response from Paradox.<br /> <br /> I think they did fantastic work reworking the Ravnos and Banu Haqim.<br /> <br /> I suppose this means that Ming Xiao is Tzimisce or the local equivalent now.</div> </div> </div> </div>But who trusts a Tzimisce to have their back, assuming they don't want their back to be full of mysterious orifices? That's the issue. Just having Kindred around means there was no one to gain anyone's confidence like a pre-KotE group could.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh you fell for that propaganda?<br /> <br /> I mean Kuei Jin doesn't even make sense linguistically! </div> </div> </div>Sure it does. You're just looking in the wrong language; check out <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dungan_language\" target=\"_blank\">Dungan</a>.<br /> <br /> (This is <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%D0%B3%D1%83%D0%B9#Dungan\" target=\"_blank\">purely by</a> <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%D0%B6%D1%8B%D0%BD#Dungan\" target=\"_blank\">accident</a>, of course.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Misinformation, my friend. The local Chinese Tzimisce are hiding their connection to the Eldest.<br /> <br /> - Malkavian Fledgling </div> </div> </div>I can't hear you over the sound of massive bear stomps.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T15:13:48-08:00","id":1555290,"title":"","content":"Was it this book? Because I picked it up, years ago, but haven't read it yet. <br /> <br /> <img width=\"732\" height=\"960\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.ebayimg.com/images/g/3K8AAeSwysNnvQf8/s-l960.webp\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.ebayimg.com/images/g/3K8AAeSwysNnvQf8/s-l960.webp\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.ebayimg.com/images/g/3K8AAeSwysNnvQf8/s-l960.webp\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T15:35:20-08:00","id":1555291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555290#post1555290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it this book? Because I picked it up, years ago, but haven't read it yet.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"732\" height=\"960\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.ebayimg.com/images/g/3K8AAeSwysNnvQf8/s-l960.webp\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.ebayimg.com/images/g/3K8AAeSwysNnvQf8/s-l960.webp\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.ebayimg.com/images/g/3K8AAeSwysNnvQf8/s-l960.webp\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I love that book.<br /> <br /> Because it was literally the opposite of almost every other of the Hunter books. The Inquisition knows EVERYTHING.<br /> <br /> Clans, Tribes, The Underworld (Hell), and some of the Traditions too.<br /> <br /> And they don't care about ANY of it.<br /> <br /> All they care about is how to kill them even with the institutional knowledge that dwarfs most of the supernaturals themselves ABOUT themselves.<br /> <br /> But no, I meant this book.<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/db/Second_Inquisition_cover.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/db/Second_Inquisition_cover.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/db/Second_Inquisition_cover.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T15:47:18-08:00","id":1555293,"title":"","content":"The Second Inquisition! Center piece of the cult comedy classic, <i>History of the World of Darkness Part II</i>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T16:09:35-08:00","id":1555296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555284#post1555284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to frown upon the western pop cultue style of vampire being universal and dominant ( although them being everywere kinda makes sense from the early modern period) but i find the idea everyone everywhere mimicking the carmarilla/ anarch status every stretches credability, slightly problamatic and frankly, boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;western&quot; vampire isn't any legend to begin with, just a pop-culture made thing, so I'm not overly worried about it in fiction.<br /> <br /> But most importantly, that's about the game and making it serviceable for the players.<br /> <br /> When you make culturally-appropriate variations elsewhere, you're not serving the players from that place, you're serving the western players with a &quot;cultural experience&quot; (that may be more or less stereotyped). It runs the risk of alienating the actual people that live in those places and want, you know, to play the game.<br /> <br /> In VtM the best version of this we ever had (and still with plenty of problems) was the Ashirra: they're a distinct political entity, but it has the same vampires and clans, it just adapts them to life in the Middle East. Even then, it's important to have a presence of the other sects in there, and also a presence of the Ashirra in the &quot;west&quot;, because players want options, especially classic options.<br /> <br /> Other &quot;localizations&quot; of Vampire, but above all KotE, run into this problem hard. Making them as culturally significant as possible meant changing several basic assumptions of the game and all but barring local players from having a classic VtM game with canon material. They had to be a foreigner's vision of their culture instead of, you know, whatever they wanted. The Drowned Legacies are maybe the least bad, although they're still pretty bad and their lore brings this all over again.<br /> <br /> So, that doesn't mean you shouldn't have cultural representation, local political movements and more types of creatures. It means you shouldn't make those things as mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555285#post1555285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if there's an actual answer that pleases everyone and I certainly don't have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Closer to that: make more options, not less.<br /> <br /> As long as the presence of Kuei-Jin don't block Asia from having regular Kindred and their sects, it wouldn't be a big problem. Let each be its own thing.<br /> <br /> In fact, it would also be interesting to have non-Asian Kuei-Jin, showing that the phenomenon isn't just a cultural tokenism, but a real thing in the WoD that happens all around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T17:41:43-08:00","id":1555300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555291#post1555291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love that book.<br /> <br /> Because it was literally the opposite of almost every other of the Hunter books. The Inquisition knows EVERYTHING.<br /> <br /> Clans, Tribes, The Underworld (Hell), and some of the Traditions too.<br /> <br /> And they don't care about ANY of it.<br /> <br /> All they care about is how to kill them even with the institutional knowledge that dwarfs most of the supernaturals themselves ABOUT themselves.<br /> <br /> But no, I meant this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, my all time favorite Inquisition-book is <i>Hunters' Hunted</i>. Teenagers vs. vampires. What could go wrong? <i>Dark Ages Inquisition</i> was kinda, well, boring. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T18:19:46-08:00","id":1555301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555300#post1555300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But, my all time favorite Inquisition-book is <i>Hunters' Hunted</i>. Teenagers vs. vampires. What could go wrong? <i>Dark Ages Inquisition</i> was kinda, well, boring.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I felt the only book that flopped was the Arcanum. But then they're academics not spies like the new AMC series tries to make them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T00:48:54-08:00","id":1555306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555296#post1555296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;western&quot; vampire isn't any legend to begin with, just a pop-culture made thing, so I'm not overly worried about it in fiction.<br /> <br /> But most importantly, that's about the game and making it serviceable for the players.<br /> <br /> When you make culturally-appropriate variations elsewhere, you're not serving the players from that place, you're serving the western players with a &quot;cultural experience&quot; (that may be more or less stereotyped). It runs the risk of alienating the actual people that live in those places and want, you know, to play the game.<br /> <br /> In VtM the best version of this we ever had (and still with plenty of problems) was the Ashirra: they're a distinct political entity, but it has the same vampires and clans, it just adapts them to life in the Middle East. Even then, it's important to have a presence of the other sects in there, and also a presence of the Ashirra in the &quot;west&quot;, because players want options, especially classic options.<br /> <br /> Other &quot;localizations&quot; of Vampire, but above all KotE, run into this problem hard. Making them as culturally significant as possible meant changing several basic assumptions of the game and all but barring local players from having a classic VtM game with canon material. They had to be a foreigner's vision of their culture instead of, you know, whatever they wanted. The Drowned Legacies are maybe the least bad, although they're still pretty bad and their lore brings this all over again.<br /> <br /> So, that doesn't mean you shouldn't have cultural representation, local political movements and more types of creatures. It means you shouldn't make those things as mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> <br /> Closer to that: make more options, not less.<br /> <br /> As long as the presence of Kuei-Jin don't block Asia from having regular Kindred and their sects, it wouldn't be a big problem. Let each be its own thing.<br /> <br /> In fact, it would also be interesting to have non-Asian Kuei-Jin, showing that the phenomenon isn't just a cultural tokenism, but a real thing in the WoD that happens all around.</div> </div> </div> </div>^THIS<br /> <br /> If you tasked me with making KotE work in modern Vampire, I'd retcon it to flip the &quot;invasion&quot; dynamic. Instead of Wan Kuei invading the American west coast recently (cringe, &quot;Yellow Peril&quot; garbage), you make the <i>Camarilla</i> invade <i>Asia</i> a century or more ago.<br /> <br /> You know, to coincide with European Colonialism.<br /> <br /> Western vampires marched into China, Japan, Korea, etc. alongside the armies of Britain, America, etc. Displacing Wan Kuei and defiling sacred spaces. Exploiting the fact that Wan Kuei are limited to however many souls claw their way up from Hell, while Kindred can Embrace without limit.<br /> <br /> Their victory wouldn't (and shouldn't) be complete. A tenuous ceasefire is reached, while both sides entrench themselves. Maybe having to keep their heads down in China during Mao's cultural revolution, where any whiff of superstition is ruthlessly stamped out by the state. Wars in Korea and Vietnam either throw nighttime warfare into disarray, or provide new avenues for settling old scores. Suffice to say, there's lots of interesting ways you could use the history of East Asia to spin 100+ years of coexistence (or lack thereof) between &quot;native&quot; and &quot;transplant&quot; vampires.<br /> <br /> What you'd have is modern nights where players could easily run EITHER kind of splat in the same locales. (Indeed, run both <i>in the same coterie</i>, if desired). Portray the two as equally viable, and equally valid.<br /> <br /> You wouldn't have a setting where an entire, rather large chunk of the planet is barred from a major splat for seemingly no reason!? It's unrealistic (Wan Kuei were capable of perfectly preventing ANY Kindred foothold in all those large, populous counties, DESPITE enduring European Colonialism, war, disease, cultural upheaval, etc?). And it's a waste of what could be a VERY interesting state of affairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T02:26:02-08:00","id":1555308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555306#post1555306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Their victory wouldn't (and shouldn't) be complete. A tenuous ceasefire is reached, while both sides entrench themselves. Maybe having to keep their heads down in China during Mao's cultural revolution, where any whiff of superstition is ruthlessly stamped out by the state. Wars in Korea and Vietnam either throw nighttime warfare into disarray, or provide new avenues for settling old scores. Suffice to say, there's lots of interesting ways you could use the history of East Asia to spin 100+ years of coexistence (or lack thereof) between &quot;native&quot; and &quot;transplant&quot; vampires.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, tho' they have their court system and very cold relationship with the locel Beast coruts, the Kuei Jin not the sole rulers of the Middle Kingdom<br /> Especially India is a hotspot where <b>Raktasadhu of India</b> (the mutual alliance of the the Daitya, Danava, Nagaraja, Eastern Ravnos, and Wu Zao against the ever-posing threat of the Kuei-jin (mostly the Infinite Thunders Court of southern India and the Golden Court of eastern India.), the Camarilla, the Ashirra, the local Sabbat and the Tzimisce Methuselah Kartarirya and her Tzimsice) have a very strong presence... and of coruse the brood of Kartarirya - who itself claimed Shri Lanka from a Nosferatu<br /> The Kin Jin have a presence in the Middle Kingdom just the KotE setting not really focuses on that, but they have a neat little rite called <b>The Way of the Lone Walker</b> what essentially makes you a &quot;Half-person&quot; not part any Court or Wu, but still part of the Kuei-jin and such &quot;Heimin&quot; main job is to act as a connection with the local Kin-jin... implying yes, there are kin-jin/Cainites in the Middle Kingdom in such numbers you need this loophole to keep contact with<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T09:09:20-08:00","id":1555315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555306#post1555306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ^THIS<br /> <br /> If you tasked me with making KotE work in modern Vampire, I'd retcon it to flip the &quot;invasion&quot; dynamic. Instead of Wan Kuei invading the American west coast recently (cringe, &quot;Yellow Peril&quot; garbage), you make the <i>Camarilla</i> invade <i>Asia</i> a century or more ago.<br /> <br /> You know, to coincide with European Colonialism.<br /> <br /> Western vampires marched into China, Japan, Korea, etc. alongside the armies of Britain, America, etc. Displacing Wan Kuei and defiling sacred spaces. Exploiting the fact that Wan Kuei are limited to however many souls claw their way up from Hell, while Kindred can Embrace without limit.<br /> <br /> Their victory wouldn't (and shouldn't) be complete. A tenuous ceasefire is reached, while both sides entrench themselves. Maybe having to keep their heads down in China during Mao's cultural revolution, where any whiff of superstition is ruthlessly stamped out by the state. Wars in Korea and Vietnam either throw nighttime warfare into disarray, or provide new avenues for settling old scores. Suffice to say, there's lots of interesting ways you could use the history of East Asia to spin 100+ years of coexistence (or lack thereof) between &quot;native&quot; and &quot;transplant&quot; vampires.<br /> <br /> What you'd have is modern nights where players could easily run EITHER kind of splat in the same locales. (Indeed, run both <i>in the same coterie</i>, if desired). Portray the two as equally viable, and equally valid.<br /> <br /> You wouldn't have a setting where an entire, rather large chunk of the planet is barred from a major splat for seemingly no reason!? It's unrealistic (Wan Kuei were capable of perfectly preventing ANY Kindred foothold in all those large, populous counties, DESPITE enduring European Colonialism, war, disease, cultural upheaval, etc?). And it's a waste of what could be a VERY interesting state of affairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that you shouldn't restrict the 13 Clans to having been European because that bleeds into the idea that they haven't been part of human history to begin with and falls prey into the European identities of them when they shouldn't have that.<br /> <br /> Mind you, that's because I always favor the idea of the Second City being equivalent to Irem in Saudi Arabia and the First City being from Africa.<br /> <br /> Because I think way too much about this.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla has a very European identity but it seems like establishing local equivalents that may eventually merge with the larger organization (the Camarilla meaning &quot;Secret Society&quot; versus actually having a name, name like the Anarchs think it does) could be a thing. The Technocracy tried to do this with the Five Metal Dragons and it wasn't....great...but I liked the idea to an extent.<br /> <br /> Just as long as it doesn't end up getting named the Jade Court or something equally exoticisized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-10-2025, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T09:18:31-08:00","id":1555316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555315#post1555315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue that you shouldn't restrict the 13 Clans to having been European because that bleeds into the idea that they haven't been part of human history to begin with and falls prey into the European identities of them when they shouldn't have that.<br /> <br /> Mind you, that's because I always favor the idea of the Second City being equivalent to Irem in Saudi Arabia and the First City being from Africa.<br /> <br /> Because I think way too much about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Africa?<br /> The First City was in the Land of Nod as far as I know<br /> The Land of Nod was located east of Eden where Caine was exiled by God after the murder of his brother Abel.<br /> Okay, just find the Garden of Eden...<br /> <br /> \u201cA river watering the garden flowed from Eden; from there it was separated into four headwaters. The name of the first is the Pishon; it winds through the entire land of Havilah, where there is gold. (The gold of that land is good; aromatic resin and onyx are also there.) The name of the second river is the Gihon; it winds through the entire land of Cush. The name of the third river is the Tigris; it runs along the east side of Ashur. And the fourth river is the Euphrates.\u201d<br /> <br /> Two of these rivers, the Tigris and Euphrates, still flow today. The Pishon and the Gihon dried up soon after the close of the last ice age. All four rivers flow or flowed into the Persian Gulf. They come close together in the southeastern part of today\u2019s Persian Gulf. Presently, this location is about 200 feet below sea level. During most of the last ice age, it was above sea level.<br /> There are many speculations about where the land of Nod may be, but it is safe to say, the Land of Nod was somewhere the area of today's Afghanistan and Pakistan - the area's geography would suit the WoD description, not to mention the First City, Enoch there in the Toreador interpretation was called Ubar, meaning &quot;Queen of Frankincense.&quot;<br /> Frankincense is an aromatic resin from the Boswellia sacra tree, and from <b>India, and the Middle East</b>, frankincense oil has been important both socially and economically as an ingredient in incense and perfumes for thousands of years<br /> Not to mention would make all those Antediluvan travels to the East much more realistic, and would explain why there is a strong Cainite presence in India to the point the Danava believe themselves to be the guardians of their Antediluvian (pitri, or &quot;father&quot;), whom they call Veddhartha. These Danava claim that the Ventrue are in fact an errant antitribu bloodline of the Danava. The Salubri say that Saulot achieved a transcendent spiritual state in the Indian city of Golconda, which falls within territory controlled by the Danava - some even believe that the very notion of Golconda originated from the Danava<br /> And why the likes of Ishtar and others migrated Westward<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, the Weeping Stone is a sacred relic and pilgrimage site for the Lost Tribe (the modern Black Hand) in the mountainous region of modern Iraq. The Black Hand believes the Stone is east of the Garden of Eden, at or near the site of the First City and the stone is Zillah (When Zillah saw that her brothers were dead and she was next, she wept and cried out to Father Caine. He heard her pleas and took pity on her, changing her into a stone so that she would not be found and killed.) The location fits<br /> Also also, Amut (Literally &quot;Eagle's Nest&quot;) Location Somewhere in Afghanistan Alamut, also known as Alah Amut (literally &quot;Eagle's Nest&quot;), is the headquarters of the Banu Haqim located somewhere in Afghanistan - and according the Banu Haqim legends it was established by Haqim himself after Khayyin almost killed him after he murdered the King and Queen of En'esh, Khe-duk and Liada and use their blood to bestow the Embrace upon himself<br /> Again the location checks out, since according their story Haqim and his followers traveled into the mountains to the southeast of the City, and it was there that they made their home, Alamut<br /> <br /> Of course this is just a theory<br /> A vampire theory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 11-10-2025, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T09:48:32-08:00","id":1555317,"title":"","content":"Consider me corrected and I choose to believe the above is from Beckett.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T13:16:43-08:00","id":1555327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555306#post1555306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you tasked me with making KotE work in modern Vampire, I'd retcon it to flip the &quot;invasion&quot; dynamic. Instead of Wan Kuei invading the American west coast recently (cringe, &quot;Yellow Peril&quot; garbage), you make the <i>Camarilla</i> invade <i>Asia</i> a century or more ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably a better dynamic, although it would have been more than 100 years ago. Europeans got in direct contact with East Asia all the way back to the 16th century, so the Camarilla could have at least a foothold since then, and the stronger &quot;colonial&quot; presence in China has about 200 years.<br /> <br /> But the presence of Kindred could be far older, as it has to do with smaller movements. Regular vampires should probably be there since ancient times or even prehistory, just like everywhere else, making for Kindred who are as much natives as the Wan Kuei.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555308#post1555308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kin Jin have a presence in the Middle Kingdom just the KotE setting not really focuses on that<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it is insipid and insufficient for Asian players who want to have a regular VtM game within the canon.<br /> <br /> Basically this just sidesteps the whole problem to say &quot;but there are some&quot;.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555315#post1555315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that you shouldn't restrict the 13 Clans to having been European because that bleeds into the idea that they haven't been part of human history to begin with and falls prey into the European identities of them when they shouldn't have that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> If anything, the 13 clans <i><b>may</b></i> have a Middle Eastern origin, if you take Noddism as gospel, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Focusing too much on their European identities was a big part of the problem, hence the Ashirra works better (and, to a lesser extent, the Indian Kindred).<br /> <br /> Even by the lore they simply aren't Europeans, it was just the game taking a lot on the same tendency of modern Catholic and Reformation churches of ignoring the existence and history of the several other branches of Christianity still alive today.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla as is is mainly an European organization by European vampires, and so is the Sabbat, but the clans existe elsewhere and have always existed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555315#post1555315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, that's because I always favor the idea of the Second City being equivalent to Irem in Saudi Arabia and the First City being from Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like to place them because I don't think they should be actual truth, but certainly this seems a reasonable placement.<br /> <br /> Caine, by the way, <i><b>wasn't white</b></i>. Not even close to it. He was either black or dark brown, on the darker side of Middle Eastern skin.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555315#post1555315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla has a very European identity but it seems like establishing local equivalents that may eventually merge with the larger organization (the Camarilla meaning &quot;Secret Society&quot; versus actually having a name, name like the Anarchs think it does) could be a thing. The Technocracy tried to do this with the Five Metal Dragons and it wasn't....great...but I liked the idea to an extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the Ashirra. And I don't think merging them was that interesting.<br /> <br /> Requiem does this with its Covenants. They certainly have an European flavor to their main presentation, but in the end they're more archetypes than anything, taking on local forms and beliefs wherever they go. WoD can't do that without a heavier <i>retcon</i>, but taking the idea and building more &quot;Ashirras&quot; would be interesting.<br /> <br /> The Metal Dragons are... complex. It makes some sense because the Union is still in no small part European Imperialism given form, they can't really work outside this context. So any branch of the organization either works under Europeans or their descendants, or under people who embrace their imperialism, and any independent version would be a spin on the same theme.<br /> <br /> With the Metal Dragons they did something like that, although it's hard to say how successful they were. It has a lot of the &quot;overly cultural representation&quot; problem, but it was a try.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555316#post1555316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Africa?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, where humanity was born.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555316#post1555316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The First City was in the Land of Nod as far as I know</div> </div> </div> </div>According to legend, you have to make a lot of assumptions for this to be the case.<br /> <br /> Even if you take Noddism as gospel, if someone want to define an actual place for it, there's no reason for it to be where a Canaanite people from about 15 centuries or more after the fall of the <i>second</i> city thought it was. There's no guarantee they even got the rivers' name correctly, or just adapted to something they actually knew.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555316#post1555316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enoch there in the Toreador interpretation was called Ubar, meaning &quot;Queen of Frankincense.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This could easily be a later legend based on anything, from a romanticization of the city to liking it to a known substance after the original one being lost to history.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555316#post1555316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention would make all those Antediluvan travels to the East much more realistic</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, because they're at the time of the <i>Second City</i>, not at the time of the First. After the Deluge (the mythical thing that was copied from the <i>Epic of Gilgamesh</i>) they could be anywhere.<br /> <br /> I think you have an argument for the First City being in the Middle East <b>if</b> you assume it's really related to the flood that actually informed the myth and vampires are of Middle Eastern origin regardless of Noddism, but in that case it would most probably be in Turkey, to the west of the four rivers instead of to the east.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555316#post1555316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and would explain why there is a strong Cainite presence in India</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> Even if Cainite legend is taken into account the Clans spread around 3000 BCE from the Second City, so the location of the First City has no bearing on this and everyone had plenty of time to reach the end of the world way before the rise of the Hebrews, not to say that the Antediluvians were wandering about while the city still existed and could Embrace whenever. As extremely potent supernatural beings they could easily travel vast distances. Even common people traveled extremely long distances at the time, only mass migrations have tighter ranges.<br /> <br /> You had Chinese products reaching Egypt before you had writing systems.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T13:34:37-08:00","id":1555432,"title":"","content":"My fellow posters have a point, vis a vis Kindred who migrated into East Asia far earlier than European Colonialism. (And also that Europeans were influencing Asian for longer than 100 years. This is why I said &quot;100+&quot;. I couldn't recall the actual timeline, so I had to set a baseline to start from.)<br /> <br /> Indeed, I imagine that, when the Camarilla (and to a lesser extent the Anarchs and Sabbat) really started making inroads in Asia, coinciding with European Imperialist forces, the native Cainites of the region almost certainly identified more with the Wan Kuei than their &quot;Western cousins&quot;. Despite that they're different supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> (Much like how, say, in India, the Christian enclaves in Kerala established in the early centuries CE probably identified culturally more with their Hindu neighbors, than with the Portuguese Catholics that arrived in the 1600s).<br /> <br /> Speaking of India, actually, one must consider how the Wan Kuei rivalry with Clan Ravnos would work. My immediate thought is that it's informed considerably more by rivalry between cultures and empires. The Wan Kuei of the Middle Kingdom don't appreciate Indian Cainites trying to muscle into their territory, for the same reason the mortals of the Middle Kingdom wouldn't appreciate armies from the subcontinent trying to conquer their lands. Once again, the problem is Imperialism.<br /> <br /> Cainites native to China and other areas, meanwhile, are broadly tolerated (to the degree that blood-sucking monsters, of any origin, &quot;tolerate&quot; anyone) because they assimilated into their local culture and power structures. Or else carved out their own power structures, and have resisted full assimilation long enough that their political positions are entrenched, with treaties and pacts and whatnot. With only the most ancient Wan Kuei remembering a time when this wasn't the case, and even that entrenched Cainite population were &quot;bastard offcomers&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla would occupy a distinctly more antagonistic force, because they came in with all the White Imperialists, kicking in their doors and demanding everything. Looting, disobeying local laws and norms, usurping local sovereignty, defiling sacred sites, and disrupting the flow of Chi. Things native Cainites know not to do, both to avoid starting fights and for their own practical benefit.<br /> <br /> From a Chronicle standpoint, this creates interesting dynamics for not only local politics in games set in East Asia, but in the options available to players. They could play as Wan Kuei pulled from the native population. As Western Kindred (pick a sect), either Embraced from transplanted Europeans or from the native population. They could be Cainites Embraced by the native Cainite population, inheriting their uniquely local flavor of the base VtM Clans/Bloodlines. (And could be either native or Western people Embraced into it). They could even play as Europeans who died, got sent a Hell(s), and clawed their way back up as Wan Kuei.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T20:38:10-08:00","id":1555453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555432#post1555432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of India, actually, one must consider how the Wan Kuei rivalry with Clan Ravnos would work. My immediate thought is that it's informed considerably more by rivalry between cultures and empires. The Wan Kuei of the Middle Kingdom don't appreciate Indian Cainites trying to muscle into their territory, for the same reason the mortals of the Middle Kingdom wouldn't appreciate armies from the subcontinent trying to conquer their lands. Once again, the problem is Imperialism.</div> </div> </div> </div>This rivalry actually makes very little sense for vampires.<br /> <br /> China and India don't have a long history of conflict. For most of history they had limited but positive contact due to the Silk Road and philosophical and religious exchanges.<br /> <br /> Only since the 18th century did their conflict started and even then it is limited to a border dispute, with very rare escalations and a single modern war that lasted one month. They mostly try to be as diplomatic as possible about the issue.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, today they're not on good terms, but it is nothing similar to what we see among vampires in the setting, not even close. It really looks like it was based on a very limited understanding of the conflict.<br /> <br /> It would make far more sense for the <b>Ravnos</b> to be in conflict with the <b>Ashirra</b> for control of areas both in India and Pakistan, or a far more limited conflict with the Wan-Kuei in the disputed border areas that vampires away from the area don't really care about. It would also be interesting to have a conflict based on traditional Indian society vs the social changes brought by the centuries of British rule, or on how the caste system changed over time in rigidity and effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T21:21:17-08:00","id":1555454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555453#post1555453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This rivalry actually makes very little sense for vampires.<br /> <br /> China and India don't have a long history of conflict. For most of history they had limited but positive contact due to the Silk Road and philosophical and religious exchanges.<br /> <br /> Only since the 18th century did their conflict started and even then it is limited to a border dispute, with very rare escalations and a single modern war that lasted one month. They mostly try to be as diplomatic as possible about the issue.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, today they're not on good terms, but it is nothing similar to what we see among vampires in the setting, not even close. It really looks like it was based on a very limited understanding of the conflict.<br /> <br /> It would make far more sense for the <b>Ravnos</b> to be in conflict with the <b>Ashirra</b> for control of areas both in India and Pakistan, or a far more limited conflict with the Wan-Kuei in the disputed border areas that vampires away from the area don't really care about. It would also be interesting to have a conflict based on traditional Indian society vs the social changes brought by the centuries of British rule, or on how the caste system changed over time in rigidity and effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit my lack of knowledge regarding the Kindred of the East is hurting me here, I assumed that the Kuei Jin fighting the Ravnos were Indian Kuei Jin fighting Ravnos and they'd been doing so for thousands of years over territory and power.<br /> <br /> Both have been there since the beginning, basically.<br /> <br /> (I have always said the Ravnos should be like the Followers of Set and believe their Antediluvian to be the First Vampire and point to their antiquity as a reason why it predates Noddism--and like the Followers of Set, it is a reasonable supposition if you ignore Generation)<br /> <br /> Certainly India and Egypt are both places you could look to as reasonable places vampirism could have begun other than the Middle East.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> One area that I think they could have hinted more at was the idea of multiple origins of the same rules. Caine was a Kuei Jin (or Revenant) that learned to spread his curse around by draining the life force of the living and transforming people. Something that could have been replicated by other people as well. Which is more Vampire: The Requiem than Vampire: The masquerade but there's a reason that everyone tends to agree that V:TR to V:TM was this meme. VTR was better written and more cohesive while more open to freedom but just lacked the gonzo and brand loyalty.<br /> <br /> At least IMHO.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"500\" height=\"516\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://imgur.com/NkwvQyU.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://imgur.com/NkwvQyU.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://imgur.com/NkwvQyU.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-14-2025, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T21:58:58-08:00","id":1555456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555454#post1555454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit my lack of knowledge regarding the Kindred of the East is hurting me here, I assumed that the Kuei Jin fighting the Ravnos were Indian Kuei Jin fighting Ravnos and they'd been doing so for thousands of years over territory and power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of but not really.<br /> <br /> There are Kuei-Jin native to India, but their territories are mostly in the east of the subcontinent. They are in a conflict with the Kin-Jin of India, but that's mostly because the other Courts pressure them to do so, and even then it is described as a Cold War at least until the Weak of Nightmares.<br /> <br /> It is the other Courts to the East (that give the India Court crap all the time) that really hate the Ravnos and use the Indian Kuei-Jin as proxy when they don't come to get personal. And they do come to get personal with some frequency because they also want to find crap on the many, many heretics in the Indian Court, the same heretics the press on waging war on the Kindred.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555454#post1555454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I have always said the Ravnos should be like the Followers of Set and believe their Antediluvian to be the First Vampire and point to their antiquity as a reason why it predates Noddism--and like the Followers of Set, it is a reasonable supposition if you ignore Generation)</div> </div> </div> </div>They are.<br /> <br /> Kindred in India in general aren't Cainites and don't give crap to the Book of Nod. And they may be on to something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555454#post1555454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One area that I think they could have hinted more at was the idea of multiple origins of the same rules. Caine was a Kuei Jin (or Revenant) that learned to spread his curse around by draining the life force of the living and transforming people. Something that could have been replicated by other people as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555454#post1555454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but there's a reason that everyone tends to agree that V:TR to V:TM was this meme. VTR was better written and more cohesive while more open to freedom but just lacked the gonzo and brand loyalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say just brand loyalty.<br /> <br /> VtR has just as much gonzo and gonzo potential, if not more, but many fans won't look at it to know. Even more at 2nd Edtion.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it's just the superior game. What it doesn't have is VtM's brand and history.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T22:26:37-08:00","id":1555458,"title":"","content":"I'd find that very offensive as an indian WOD fan as the Indian Kuei Jin should certainly be able to exert their own power and reasons for war. I don't recall any period in history that India was under the control of China either.<br /> <br /> Mind you, if you wanted to get uncomfortable (and why would you?), you'd think the Ashirra and the Ravnos would be at each other's throats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555456#post1555456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seriously, it's just the superior game. What it doesn't have is VtM's brand and history.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it's the fact that my loyalty to VTM is due to the characters. 5th Edition is uninterested in them, though, with the exception of the spin off material like the New York games and LA by Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T22:55:22-08:00","id":1555459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555454#post1555454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> (I have always said the Ravnos should be like the Followers of Set and believe their Antediluvian to be the First Vampire and point to their antiquity as a reason why it predates Noddism--and like the Followers of Set, it is a reasonable supposition if you ignore Generation)<br /> <br /> One area that I think they could have hinted more at was the idea of multiple origins of the same rules. Caine was a Kuei Jin (or Revenant) that learned to spread his curse around by draining the life force of the living and transforming people. Something that could have been replicated by other people as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The interesting/funny thing is... Nodism, the Book of Nod itself support this!<br /> I mean the Book of Nod literally says: &quot;By calling up demons and listening to whispered wisdom he learned the way to make a child of his own.&quot; after detailing how Lilith helped him, implying Caine was not only a Ravenant but an infernalist, a proto-baali so to speak...<br /> <br /> So if you go with that?<br /> The multiple Vampire races are plausible<br /> We have <b>Caine/Khayyin</b> [VtM] and his strange brood who are from the Kuei-jin point of view are barely more than a chih-mei (and the Nagaraja need to consume flesh echoes their &quot;origin&quot;)<br /> <b>The Bloody Man</b> [Silver Records]\u200b who probably some ancient monstrosity of proto-vampires; kind of the cro-magnon version of Vampires<br /> We have the <b>Asuras</b> of the Khara who are may or may not be the spawns of the Bloody Man, but probably their own seperate dark race<br /> <b>Cagn</b> [Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom]\u200b , and the Ebony Kingdom even supports further there are other Vampires than them, because several Legacies like one of the Main, the Ishtary are self admitedly from outside the Ebony Kingdom and not part of Cagn family<br /> <b>Canarl</b> [Wolves of the Sea]\u200b his people, the Einherjar are a lovely addition to the game anyhow, and with their fixation to prepare the Ragnarok and be Odin's chosen warriors who will be able to shape the future are the treasuretrove of Vampire race-wars<br /> <b>Zapathasura</b> [Clanbook Ravnos]\u200b and the Ravnos, who were made to replace and combat the asuratizayya or &quot;countless demons&quot; (Kuei-jin) who faild their tasks, but similarly failed<br /> <b>Bonsam</b> [Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition]. The first of the Bonsam claims to have never actually been Embraced, having been brought to unlife by a darkness from before creation<br /> <b>Sutekh/Set</b> [Clanbook Settite]\u200b and his people who may or may not the Kuei-jin equivalent of Egypt<br /> <br /> It is a fun can of worms to unpack or explore actually<br /> <br /> And as an extra, Dark Ages mentions, where Nodism was absent and christianity not really spread, and mostly during the antiquitie we had <b>Ixion</b> and vampire belived they were the descendants of Ixion.\u200b \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T23:19:20-08:00","id":1555460,"title":"","content":"In my homebrew games, I had Hecate as believed to be the first vampire. She and the Eriynes desired worship of their own and stole souls from Hades that they gave immortality and amborsia before setting up their own kingdom in Atlantis. The gods, being the gods, were furious and cursed the first vampires by deluging their city and then each laying a curse upon one of them.<br /> <br /> <i>The Book of Hecate</i>, which my players had found, said not only were there more than 13 founders but that the various Clan Founders decreed that they would attempt to appease the gods by being like the gods who had cursed them. The exceptions being the Helios cursed Typhon who turned to the worship of the Scourge of the Gods in hopes of getting revenge and the Vestian cursed Echidnans who vowed they would unleash monsters onto mankind for the rest of time.<br /> <br /> In the game, Beckett pointed out that a lot of Noddist ideas were similar to the ones in the Book of Hecate and he wondered if the Jewish version was actually a modification of the Greek legends than the reverse once the Hellenistic conquest happened.<br /> <br /> Brujah: Athenans/Aresians (two bloodlines)<br /> Banu Haqim: Eriynes (for the three castes)<br /> Cappadocian: Hadeans<br /> Followers of Set: Typhons<br /> Gangrel: Artemin<br /> Lasombra: Nyxians<br /> Malkavian: Maenads<br /> Nosferatu: Hephaestus<br /> Ravnos: Hermes<br /> Salubri: Apollyn<br /> Toreador: Aphros<br /> Tzimisce: Echidna<br /> Ventrue: Zeusian<br /> <br /> I had the implication be for my campaigns that there were actually a lot of these, &quot;similar to the Book of Nod but different&quot; texts lying around Kindred society rather than just the Book of Nod being the one. Of course, in my games, I also had the Book of Nod allegedly written by Cappadocias as he was the Antediluvian who had converted to Christianity and was also insane, framing everything that he supposedly remembered happening through the framework of Abrahmic religion. There was also allegedly a second Book of Nod that was written on the interior of Saulot's tomb which was roughly the same stories that Cappadocias shared but different names which the Tremere wrote down.<br /> <br /> This is the only &quot;proof&quot; that the Noddist version is more true than any others. But talk to local vampires and virtually every culture has their own version of the First Vampire, Flood, 13 assholes, and betrayal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-14-2025, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T23:41:21-08:00","id":1555461,"title":"","content":"Well, probably not everyone has a version of the flood. That didn't happen everywhere by a long shot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555459#post1555459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The interesting/funny thing is... Nodism, the Book of Nod itself support this!<br /> I mean the Book of Nod literally says: &quot;By calling up demons and listening to whispered wisdom he learned the way to make a child of his own.&quot; after detailing how Lilith helped him, implying Caine was not only a Ravenant but an infernalist, a proto-baali so to speak...<br /> <br /> So if you go with that?<br /> The multiple Vampire races are plausible<br /> We have <b>Caine/Khayyin</b> [VtM] and his strange brood who are from the Kuei-jin point of view are barely more than a chih-mei (and the Nagaraja need to consume flesh echoes their &quot;origin&quot;)<br /> <b>The Bloody Man</b> [Silver Records] who probably some ancient monstrosity of proto-vampires; kind of the cro-magnon version of Vampires</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know that you wouldn't really be able to tell the difference between a Cro-Magnon and a human off the street, right? Maybe the former might be slightly more likely to have room for wisdom teeth in their skulls, but otherwise, Cro-Magnon were anatomically modern <i>Homo sapiens sapiens</i>. Also, The Silver Record probably doesn't place that figure that far back; if we're going by Shattered Dreams, vampires weren't seemingly an issue until many generations after humans discover how to form gold and silver. Even if their origin goes back further, vampires would have been behind the scenes and quite literally slumbering for tens of thousands of years before they got out in significant number.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And as an extra, Dark Ages mentions, where Nodism was absent and christianity not really spread, and mostly during the antiquitie we had <b>Ixion</b> and vampire belived they were the descendants of Ixion. \u200b </div> </div> </div>Vampires seem to have the collective consistency of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Tetz8qMx9ro\" target=\"_blank\">Crow T. Robot</a> when it comes to forming their identities. Alternately, standard &quot;I'm the god!&quot; complex at work, claiming to be whatever deity is popular to whomever will listen because you concentrated blood a bit and think that commanding humans with Dominate makes you the Dark Lord of the Night Eternal.<br /> <br /> Or both. Both. Both is good.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T23:45:07-08:00","id":1555464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555461#post1555461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do know that you wouldn't really be able to tell the difference between a Cro-Magnon and a human off the street, right? Maybe the former might be slightly more likely to have room for wisdom teeth in their skulls, but otherwise, Cro-Magnon were anatomically modern <i>Homo sapiens sapiens</i>.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I ment to write <i>Neanderthals</i>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T00:24:53-08:00","id":1555465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555461#post1555461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, probably not everyone has a version of the flood. That didn't happen everywhere by a long shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's absolutely in everyone's version of the Book of Nod, though. Though sometimes its an Earthquake, Volcano, or other natural disaster.<br /> <br /> Mostly because the point is to establish this is an event that happens and the retellings are of a RL one.<br /> <br /> Or at least that was my ST thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T04:29:08-08:00","id":1555470,"title":"","content":"If you go with the interpretation that The Flood was the filling of the Black Sea in roughly 5600 BC, means you have the residents of the First City scattering east and west across the Steppe, and south into the Mediterranian/Middle East, at just about the dawn of the first multi city civilisations, and that the Moskva may have settled on someone you really don't want to wake up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T10:59:16-08:00","id":1555473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555458#post1555458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd find that very offensive as an indian WOD fan as the Indian Kuei Jin should certainly be able to exert their own power and reasons for war. I don't recall any period in history that India was under the control of China either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actively searched for something just in case, there's nothing. They literally only started this border problem by the 18th century and it's just about some border territories, nothing major to their respective sizes. They don't even want to commit to an actual war because of that, and in fact don't want it to spoil BRICS, so take from that what you will.<br /> <br /> And I agree, the whole thing is pretty weird and probably offensive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555458#post1555458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, if you wanted to get uncomfortable (and why would you?), you'd think the Ashirra and the Ravnos would be at each other's throats.</div> </div> </div> </div>The history of the Muslim/Hindu feud in India is recent, but far more compelling, and actually makes sense to be brought into the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555458#post1555458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, it's the fact that my loyalty to VTM is due to the characters. 5th Edition is uninterested in them, though, with the exception of the spin off material like the New York games and LA by Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just calling everything brand loyalty for simplicity's sake.<br /> <br /> Just so we don't mistake loyalty to the particular lore you know for the notion that a given lore is superior (which may still be your opinion, but I prefer to have those concepts distinct).<br /> <br /> But yeah, VtM (and WoD in general) has a lot of pull through the attachment to lore and characters.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555460#post1555460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my homebrew games, I had Hecate as believed to be the first vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll steal this and make my own modifications, thanks!\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555461#post1555461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, The Silver Record probably doesn't place that figure that far back; if we're going by Shattered Dreams, vampires weren't seemingly an issue until many generations after humans discover how to form gold and silver. Even if their origin goes back further, vampires would have been behind the scenes and quite literally slumbering for tens of thousands of years before they got out in significant number.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that what makes Vampires be what they are now for Shapechangers is their society.<br /> <br /> In a world before they formed their &quot;First City&quot; (for whatever it really was) and the Earth was even more widespread with weird species (including supernatural ones) and unique monsters, vampires would hardly be identified as a specific phenomenon.<br /> <br /> So it is perfectly possible that vampire-like entities have existed for a far longer time, even actual Kindred could be older than Early Modern Humans, and yet they wouldn't appear in the Silver Record and even Mnesis would have trouble distinguishing them from background noise.<br /> <br /> We could have a very interesting crossover chronicle based on the idea that the Kindred condition isn't actually exclusively human and has been hidden in the wild since the era of the Dragon Kings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555461#post1555461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternately, standard &quot;I'm the god!&quot; complex at work, claiming to be whatever deity is popular to whomever will listen because you concentrated blood a bit and think that commanding humans with Dominate makes you the Dark Lord of the Night Eternal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much. Most characters actually aren't like that, even among Elders and Methuselah.<br /> <br /> But those who are, they get quite famous and their names are repeated <i>ad nauseam</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T11:39:37-08:00","id":1555475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555458#post1555458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, it's the fact that my loyalty to VTM is due to the characters. 5th Edition is uninterested in them, though, with the exception of the spin off material like the New York games and LA by Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I ever decide to study TRPGs in an academic setting again, one of the things I've considered researching is players' relationship with lore and canon. I think it's interesting that the TRPG IPs with the deepest lore are all somewhat contemporaneous (<i>World of Darkness</i>, <i>Shadowrun</i>, and <i>Cyberpunk</i> all released within 3-4 years of each other). The sheer volume of depth in the World of Darkness and its overwhelming popularity created a brand loyalty that sets it apart from almost any other game. I'm really curious how the &quot;average&quot; WoD player adheres to existing lore and how it's different from the players who are more tightly bound to specific communities like this one. And I'd also love to see how it's being played differently between legacy fans and newer fans brought on in the Paradox era. Of course, like all TRPG studies, it's really hard to get at a representative sample.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T18:44:25-08:00","id":1555485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>higgipedia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555475#post1555475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's interesting that the TRPG IPs with the deepest lore are all somewhat contemporaneous (<i>World of Darkness</i>, <i>Shadowrun</i>, and <i>Cyberpunk</i> all released within 3-4 years of each other).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if this observation is accurate.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D started with the idea of being lore agnostic, but fans requested from the get go to have more of it, leading to the creation of the <i>Greyhawk</i> setting. <i>T\u00e9kumel</i> had huge lore from the get go in 1975 and was a great success (it didn't got far due to internal issues at TSR). <i>Chivalry &amp; Sorcery</i> also had a profound investment in lore in 1976. <i>Champions</i> brought deeper lore to the Super Hero genre in 1981. Chaosium brought more lines with careful lore, either from scratch or advancing from previous literature, with games like <i>RuneQuest, Stormbringer</i> and <i>Call of Cthulhu</i>. Even <i>Paranoia</i> got a lot of lore starting from it's first core book in 1984, and most of <i>Mage</i> lore started out from <i>Ars Magica</i> in 1987. All that without including those who already start from lore heavy franchises despite not advancing them much, and games who tried to start a deeper lore but didn't went far for other reasons, who existed at least since <i>Star Trek</i> in 1978.<br /> <br /> RPGs with deep lore existed from the beginning and kept coming up after. In this regard, I don't see <i>World of Darkness</i>, <i>Shadowrun</i> and <i>Cyberpunk</i> as special (despite the first two being really good, but I find the third unimpressive). WoD is a special case in how much momentum it got during the 90s, but that's about how many sourcebooks and stuff it churned out than being different in concept.<br /> <br /> Maybe the perception that they stand up to players from the 90s and later is a more relevant investigation to begin with, instead of an assumption to start a research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-15T12:30:15-08:00","id":1555492,"title":"","content":"I know this is somewhat tangential to the original point of this thread, but jumping off from the KotE talk, I always try to take the opportunity to proselytize for this one really neat (IMO) thread reimagining them that someone did a couple years ago on the RPG. Net forum. Give it a gander if that might interest you!<br /> <br /> X <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/kindred-of-the-east-the-relentless-age-live-drafting-a-final-reboot.893999/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...reboot.893999/</a><br /> <br /> (If you like it, they did a similar thread reimagining the Hsien for CtD that I also thought was cool)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T17:16:14-08:00","id":1555616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was?p=1555492#post1555492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that someone did a couple years ago on the RPG. Net forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>The someone in question is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13580_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13580\" data-vbnamecard=\"13580\">Hsienfan</a>. I didn't read the thread for my own reasons, but I did heard it's good from a lot of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T11:24:05-08:00","id":1555637,"title":"","content":"Oh I didn\u2019t realize they were on this forum too! Thank you for shouting them out here Monteparnas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T03:31:04-08:00","id":1555790,"title":"","content":"my idea for the kuei jin was they'd be linked with the Dharmic religions rather than asian ethnicities explaining their geographical and cultural aspects. This would allow a larger degree of flexibility while removing some of the problematic elements (An idea I had for white kuei jin was Cults who misappropriate dharmic religions) . For example Malaysia would be held by the ashirra and their would be a increasing presence of kuei jin in western nations due to be immigration and the proliferation of dharmic religions. Combined with the kindred riding the colonial age to set up domains through force and it'd be comparatively easy to have your cake and eat it in terms of kindred/kuei jin presence<br /> <br /> To develop it further I'd a write up on how south asia kuei jin (they probably have another name) are cultural distinct from the more obvious chinese influenced corebook types as well as trying to figure who owns what, not to mention taking this mindset further and having other species of vampire present in other countries-eg some sort of Siberian undead which is near extinction due to kindred pressure.<br /> Once idea I played with was having Y\u016brei as their own distinct sub-type of undead in japan for example and being notoriously hard to kill so surviving pressure from the other two types of undead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-23-2025, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T22:21:56-08:00","id":1557401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554743-i-think-my-issue-with-the-second-inquisition-was#post1554743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The recent thread I made on how the Second Inquisition could end had me thinking about what the intentions were for the organization versus the expectations of fans.<br /> <br /> I had a problem with THE SECOND INQUISITION book and why I realized that I'd been reading the writer's intentions all along. Basically, for a lot of fans, the Second Inquisition was this massive police state organization that would be able to track down and systematically eliminate vampires across the globe via anonymous military strikes during the day and burning the buildings down around them. It's a horrifying situation that means that vampire society has to cease to exist.<br /> <br /> It's not that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even if it isn't, that seems to be how they're portrayed in table top. I have yet to find a single live play session where the Second Inquisition wasn't presented in a way where the vampires are completely screwed as soon as they show up. This problem also existed in Swansong, as you never get the option to just go buck wild and slaughter them. It's always you having to sneak your way around their forces, or in the case of Emem, stealth killing them from the vents. Caleb can't even mind control them, because they're wearing sound proof visors or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, it's laughable that the SI only started to get its act together after the breach of Schrecknet. Because yeah, that's why the Society of Leopold failed to wipe out the vampire menace... lack of government support. Even through they were a church funded organization who had agencies all over the globe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}